 {
  "id": 24,
  "platform": "NES",
  "game": "Kirby's Adventure",
  "target": "Rainbow Resort",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Kirby%27s_Adventure/Walkthrough",
  "section_count": 7,
  "description": "Rainbow Resort, Kirby's Adventure (NES). However, there is a secret in this area: some of the blue blocks that border the path are actually destructible. The last area is very easy and straightforward. Vacuum the star blocks under the Shotzos to make them fall and head to the exit door at the bottom.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Rainbow Resort' from Kirby's Adventure (NES). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Rainbow Resort, Kirby's Adventure (NES). However, there is a secret in this area: some of the blue blocks that border the path are actually destructible. The last area is very easy and straightforward. Vacuum the star blocks under the Shotzos to make them fall and head to the exit door at the bottom. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "At the beginning of the level you have the possibility to acquire the Laser skill. Acquire it to easily eliminate all enemies along the path by bouncing it off inclined surfaces. Just before the door it will also allow you to take a 1-Up. In the next area you have to fight your way along a path of star blocks. Shortly after starting, you have the opportunity to acquire the Fire or Spark skill, which will allow you to proceed more quickly. Continuing, you have the opportunity to take a Pep Drink. However, there is a secret in this area: some of the blue blocks that border the path are actually destructible. Just below where you find a Flamer, you can destroy the blocks on the floor, using Spark or a slide attack. You will thus be able to reach a compartment in which there is a Waddle Doo, from which you can acquire the Beam skill. At this point, continue along the path. When you get to a ",
  "brief": "Rainbow Resort, Kirby's Adventure (NES). However, there is a secret in this area: some of the blue blocks that border the path are actually destructible. The last area is very easy and straightforward. Vacuum the star blocks under the Shotzos to make them fall and head to the exit door at the bottom.",
  "page_title": "Kirby's Adventure/Rainbow Resort",
  "image_url": "https://cdn.wikimg.net/en/strategywiki/images/4/4e/Kirby%27s_Adventure_King_Dedede.png",
  "image_kind": "screenshot",
  "image_urls": [
