 {
  "id": 25,
  "platform": "NES",
  "game": "EarthBound Beginnings",
  "target": "Magicant",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/EarthBound_Beginnings/Walkthrough",
  "section_count": 2,
  "description": "Magicant, EarthBound Beginnings (NES). A North American version of the game was localized into English under the monikerEarth Bound, but was eventually abandoned as commercially nonviable. A copy of this prototype was later found and circulated on the Internet under the informal titleEarthBound Zero. This is the first game in theMotherseries.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Magicant' from EarthBound Beginnings (NES). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Magicant, EarthBound Beginnings (NES). A North American version of the game was localized into English under the monikerEarth Bound, but was eventually abandoned as commercially nonviable. A copy of this prototype was later found and circulated on the Internet under the informal titleEarthBound Zero. This is the first game in theMotherseries. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "This is the first game in theMotherseries. For other games in the series see theMother category. EarthBound Beginnings, known asEarth Boundin-game and in Japan asMother, is anRPGdeveloped byApeandPax Softnicaand published byNintendofor theFamicomin1989. It is the first entry in theMotherseries. It is modeled on the gameplay of theDragon Questseries, but is set in the late 20th-century United States, unlike its fantasy genre contemporaries. Writer and director Shigesato Itoi pitchedMother's concept to Shigeru Miyamoto while visiting Nintendo's headquarters for other business. Though Miyamoto rejected the proposal at first, he eventually gave Itoi a development team. A North American version of the game was localized into English under the monikerEarth Bound, but was eventually abandoned as commercially nonviable. A copy of this prototype was later found and circulated on the Internet unde",
  "brief": "Magicant, EarthBound Beginnings (NES). A North American version of the game was localized into English under the monikerEarth Bound, but was eventually abandoned as commercially nonviable. A copy of this prototype was later found and circulated on the Internet under the informal titleEarthBound Zero. This is the first game in theMotherseries.",
  "page_title": "EarthBound Beginnings",
  "image_url": "https://cdn.wikimg.net/en/strategywiki/images/thumb/5/54/Nintendo_Power_Earth_Bound_Preview.png/800px-Nintendo_Power_Earth_Bound_Preview.png",
  "image_kind": "screenshot",
