  "section_count": 1,
  "description": "Forest of Illusion, Super Mario World (SNES). One leads to Roy's Castle, which in turn leads to the next world. The Forest of Illusion is a convoluted maze of paths and levels. There are two paths that lead out of the area.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Forest of Illusion' from Super Mario World (SNES). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Forest of Illusion, Super Mario World (SNES). One leads to Roy's Castle, which in turn leads to the next world. The Forest of Illusion is a convoluted maze of paths and levels. There are two paths that lead out of the area. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "The Forest of Illusion is a convoluted maze of paths and levels. If you just go to the straight path, you will simply go into circles. You will need to find the secret exits if you want to get out of this area - and there are lots of secret exits in this world. There are two paths that lead out of the area. One leads to Roy's Castle, which in turn leads to the next world. The other path leads to the fortress, and beating it enables another uplink to Star Road.",
