  "platform": "SNES",
  "game": "Secret of Mana",
  "target": "The Mana Fortress",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Secret_of_Mana/Walkthrough",
  "section_count": 1,
  "description": "The Mana Fortress, Secret of Mana (SNES). Secret of Mana, originally released in Japan asSeiken Densetsu 2(聖剣伝説2), is a1993actionrole-playing gamedeveloped and published bySquare(nowSquare Enix) for theSNES. It is the sequel to the1991game Seiken Densetsu, released in North America asFinal Fantasy Adventureand in Europe as Mystic Quest, and it was the first Seiken Densetsu title to be marketed as part of the Mana series rather than the Final Fantasy series.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'The Mana Fortress' from Secret of Mana (SNES). The attached reference image is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: The Mana Fortress, Secret of Mana (SNES). Secret of Mana, originally released in Japan asSeiken Densetsu 2(聖剣伝説2), is a1993actionrole-playing gamedeveloped and published bySquare(nowSquare Enix) for theSNES. It is the sequel to the1991game Seiken Densetsu, released in North America asFinal Fantasy Adventureand in Europe as Mystic Quest, and it was the first Seiken Densetsu title to be marketed as part of the Mana series rather than the Final Fantasy series. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "Secret of Mana, originally released in Japan asSeiken Densetsu 2(聖剣伝説2), is a1993actionrole-playing gamedeveloped and published bySquare(nowSquare Enix) for theSNES. It is the sequel to the1991game Seiken Densetsu, released in North America asFinal Fantasy Adventureand in Europe as Mystic Quest, and it was the first Seiken Densetsu title to be marketed as part of the Mana series rather than the Final Fantasy series. Secret of Mana was directed and designed by Koichi Ishii, programmed primarily by Nasir Gebelli, and produced by veteran Square designer Hiromichi Tanaka. The original version was re-released for the Wii'sVirtual Consolein 2008. The game was ported to mobile phones in Japan in 2009, and an enhanced port of the game was released for iOS in 2010 and Android in 2014. A 3D remake of the game was released for PlayStation 4, PlayStation Vita, and Microsoft Windows on February 15, 2",
  "brief": "The Mana Fortress, Secret of Mana (SNES). Secret of Mana, originally released in Japan asSeiken Densetsu 2(聖剣伝説2), is a1993actionrole-playing gamedeveloped and published bySquare(nowSquare Enix) for theSNES. It is the sequel to the1991game Seiken Densetsu, released in North America asFinal Fantasy Adventureand in Europe as Mystic Quest, and it was the first Seiken Densetsu title to be marketed as part of the Mana series rather than the Final Fantasy series.",
  "page_title": "Secret of Mana",
  "image_url": null,
  "image_kind": null
 },
