  "section_count": 2,
  "description": "Turtle Village, Golden Axe (Genesis). The game was well received at the time of release, Golden Axe was later converted for play on many different home systems, including Sega's ownMega Drive/GenesisandMaster System. This is the first game in theGolden Axeseries. For other games in the series see theGolden Axe category.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Turtle Village' from Golden Axe (Genesis). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Turtle Village, Golden Axe (Genesis). The game was well received at the time of release, Golden Axe was later converted for play on many different home systems, including Sega's ownMega Drive/GenesisandMaster System. This is the first game in theGolden Axeseries. For other games in the series see theGolden Axe category. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "This is the first game in theGolden Axeseries. For other games in the series see theGolden Axe category. Golden Axeis a side-scrolling hack-and-slash game released bySegaforarcadesin1989, running on the Sega System 16B arcade hardware. Makoto Uchida was the lead designer of the game, and was also responsible for the creation of the previous year'sAltered Beast. The game casts players as one of three warriors who must free the fantastical land of Yuria from the tyrannical rule of Death Adder, who wields the titular Golden Axe. The game was well received at the time of release, Golden Axe was later converted for play on many different home systems, including Sega's ownMega Drive/GenesisandMaster System. The game's success spawned an entire franchise consisting of several sequels and various spin-offs.",
  "brief": "Turtle Village, Golden Axe (Genesis). The game was well received at the time of release, Golden Axe was later converted for play on many different home systems, including Sega's ownMega Drive/GenesisandMaster System. This is the first game in theGolden Axeseries. For other games in the series see theGolden Axe category.",
