  "id": 80,
  "platform": "Genesis",
  "game": "Disney's Aladdin",
  "target": "Agrabah Rooftops",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Disney%27s_Aladdin_(Sega)/Walkthrough",
  "section_count": 0,
  "description": "Agrabah Rooftops, Disney's Aladdin (Genesis). The gameplay is a platformer at heart, centering around navigating obstacles, collecting items, and defeating enemies with either apples or a sword. Disney's Aladdinis a platform action game created byVirgin InteractiveandWalt Disney Computer Software. Disney's own animators worked on the visuals, resulting in locations and characters that look just as they do in the film itself.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Agrabah Rooftops' from Disney's Aladdin (Genesis). The attached reference image is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Agrabah Rooftops, Disney's Aladdin (Genesis). The gameplay is a platformer at heart, centering around navigating obstacles, collecting items, and defeating enemies with either apples or a sword. Disney's Aladdinis a platform action game created byVirgin InteractiveandWalt Disney Computer Software. Disney's own animators worked on the visuals, resulting in locations and characters that look just as they do in the film itself. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "Disney's Aladdinis a platform action game created byVirgin InteractiveandWalt Disney Computer Software. The gameplay is a platformer at heart, centering around navigating obstacles, collecting items, and defeating enemies with either apples or a sword. Disney's own animators worked on the visuals, resulting in locations and characters that look just as they do in the film itself. Virgin used a special \"Digicel\" process to convert the animation cels into a form the Genesis could handle while still maintaining the visual fluidity. The game's success on the Genesis led to it being ported to the Amiga, NES, Game Boy, Game Boy Color, and MS-DOS. There was also a bootleg arcade board released based on the Japanese Mega Drive version, as well as a Famicom bootleg with some gameplay differences. See theversionspage for details of the different versions created. The game's storyline follows the m",
  "brief": "Agrabah Rooftops, Disney's Aladdin (Genesis). The gameplay is a platformer at heart, centering around navigating obstacles, collecting items, and defeating enemies with either apples or a sword. Disney's Aladdinis a platform action game created byVirgin InteractiveandWalt Disney Computer Software. Disney's own animators worked on the visuals, resulting in locations and characters that look just as they do in the film itself.",
  "page_title": "Disney's Aladdin",
  "image_url": null,
  "image_kind": null
 },
