  "description": "Alien Wasteland, Another World (Genesis). Another World was innovative in its use of cinematic effects in the graphics, sound and cut scenes, with characters communicating through their facial features, gestures, and actions only. This is the first game in theAnother Worldseries. For other games in the series see theAnother World category.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Alien Wasteland' from Another World (Genesis). World brief: Alien Wasteland, Another World (Genesis). Another World was innovative in its use of cinematic effects in the graphics, sound and cut scenes, with characters communicating through their facial features, gestures, and actions only. This is the first game in theAnother Worldseries. For other games in the series see theAnother World category. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "This is the first game in theAnother Worldseries. For other games in the series see theAnother World category. Another World, known asOut of This Worldin North America andOuter Worldin Japan, is a1991cinematicplatformerdesigned and developed by Eric Chahi. The graphics and box art were designed by Chahi, while the music was composed by Jean-François Freitas. Another World was innovative in its use of cinematic effects in the graphics, sound and cut scenes, with characters communicating through their facial features, gestures, and actions only. This cinematic style granted Another World cult status amongst critics and fans. Originally developed on an Amiga 500 for theCommodore Amiga,Atari ST,Apple IIGSandMS-DOSplatforms, the game was widely ported to other contemporary systems. Later efforts resulted in several game engine recreations for the game that permitted it to run on modern comput",
