  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Pac-Man/Walkthrough",
  "section_count": 8,
  "description": "The Neon Labyrinth, Pac-Man (Arcade). Atari snapped up the rights to bring the arcade hit home, and let down millions of fans with a sub-par conversion on what was their most popular home system at the time, the Atari 2600. Despite Pac-Man's popularity, no official explanation has ever been provided by Namco as to why Pac-Man has to run around a maze, gobble the pellets, and avoid the ghosts. This is the first game in thePac-Manseries.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'The Neon Labyrinth' from Pac-Man (Arcade). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: The Neon Labyrinth, Pac-Man (Arcade). Atari snapped up the rights to bring the arcade hit home, and let down millions of fans with a sub-par conversion on what was their most popular home system at the time, the Atari 2600. Despite Pac-Man's popularity, no official explanation has ever been provided by Namco as to why Pac-Man has to run around a maze, gobble the pellets, and avoid the ghosts. This is the first game in thePac-Manseries. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "This is the first game in thePac-Manseries. For other games in the series see thePac-Man category. Inspired over a lunch of pizza,Pac-Man(originally entitledPuckmanin Japanese) began life in the arcades in1980. It was designed by Toru Iwatani, who had previously designed theGee Beetrilogy, and was the first Namco game to incorporate a four-way joystick. After being overlooked by \"experts\" who judged Namco's ownRally-Xto be the better of the two games, Pac-Man went on to unprecedented success and became an icon in Japan and in America. Pac-Man's game play was a stark and refreshing contrast to the space aged shoot'em ups that were popular at the time. Pac-mania became a phenomenon and video games' first mascot was met with an insatiable demand. Atari snapped up the rights to bring the arcade hit home, and let down millions of fans with a sub-par conversion on what was their most popular h",
  "brief": "The Neon Labyrinth, Pac-Man (Arcade). Atari snapped up the rights to bring the arcade hit home, and let down millions of fans with a sub-par conversion on what was their most popular home system at the time, the Atari 2600. Despite Pac-Man's popularity, no official explanation has ever been provided by Namco as to why Pac-Man has to run around a maze, gobble the pellets, and avoid the ghosts. This is the first game in thePac-Manseries.",
