  "description_raw": "This is the first game in theBattlezoneseries. For other games in the series see theBattlezone category. Battlezoneis a first-personshooterarcade game which was released byAtariin1980; it utilizes one Motorola M6502 (running at 1.512 MHz), with a Pokey sound chip running at that same speed, and a custom DAC. It was later ported to several other systems, and was included in several compilations - and common play in the U.S. can range from $0.25 to $1 per game (depending on how the cabinet is set). The default setting is $0.25 play with three lives and two bonuses at 15,000 and 100,000 points.",
