  "game": "Frogger",
  "target": "Highway & Waterway",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Frogger",
  "page_title": "Frogger",
  "section_count": 2,
  "description": "Highway & Waterway, Frogger (More Atari 2600). As such, they joined the race withAtari, and laterColeco, to acquire the home conversion rights to several popular arcade hits. Along withQ*BertandPopeye, they scored the rights to release Q*Bert for home systems and computers. This is the first game in theFroggerseries.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Highway & Waterway' from Frogger (More Atari 2600). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Highway & Waterway, Frogger (More Atari 2600). As such, they joined the race withAtari, and laterColeco, to acquire the home conversion rights to several popular arcade hits. Along withQ*BertandPopeye, they scored the rights to release Q*Bert for home systems and computers. This is the first game in theFroggerseries. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "This is the first game in theFroggerseries. For other games in the series see theFrogger category. Froggerwas a product of the popularization of \"cute\" games throughout1981that moved away from alien and explosion themes. In the game, you must direct a frog through traffic, and across a crowded river, and in to one of five enclosures at the top of the screen. Frogger isn't credited with many innovations, but it did break ground in continuous background music that changed contextually based on the action in the game. In1982, Parker Brothers was determined to become a major player in the video game industry. As such, they joined the race withAtari, and laterColeco, to acquire the home conversion rights to several popular arcade hits. Along withQ*BertandPopeye, they scored the rights to release Q*Bert for home systems and computers. In an ironic twist, they only acquired the rights to publis",
  "brief": "Highway & Waterway, Frogger (More Atari 2600). As such, they joined the race withAtari, and laterColeco, to acquire the home conversion rights to several popular arcade hits. Along withQ*BertandPopeye, they scored the rights to release Q*Bert for home systems and computers. This is the first game in theFroggerseries.",
