  "description": "Mountain Tunnel Slices, Vanguard (More Atari 2600). Vanguard was an exciting and visually impressive game, but it was lost among the competition that came out around the same time. That did not stopAtarifrom buying the license to distribute the game on home systems. Vanguardwas an arcade game of many firsts.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Mountain Tunnel Slices' from Vanguard (More Atari 2600). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Mountain Tunnel Slices, Vanguard (More Atari 2600). Vanguard was an exciting and visually impressive game, but it was lost among the competition that came out around the same time. That did not stopAtarifrom buying the license to distribute the game on home systems. Vanguardwas an arcade game of many firsts. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "Vanguardwas an arcade game of many firsts. It was developed in1981byTOSE, and it was SNK's first color game. It also included a synthesized voice. It was one of the first horizontally scrolling shooters, and the first that allowed the player to fire in four directions independently of the ship's motion. Finally, it's the first game to incorporate the concept of a boss, a final opponent at the end of the game that is more difficult to beat than usual. Vanguard was an exciting and visually impressive game, but it was lost among the competition that came out around the same time. That did not stopAtarifrom buying the license to distribute the game on home systems. However, they only opted to bring it to their ownAtari 2600andAtari 5200systems. A hacked 5200 version was also released on theAtari 8-bithome computers. Vanguard was an ambitious title for the 2600, and given the system's limitat",
  "brief": "Mountain Tunnel Slices, Vanguard (More Atari 2600). Vanguard was an exciting and visually impressive game, but it was lost among the competition that came out around the same time. That did not stopAtarifrom buying the license to distribute the game on home systems. Vanguardwas an arcade game of many firsts.",
