  "id": 115,
  "platform": "More Atari 2600",
  "game": "Crystal Castles",
  "target": "Isometric Honeycomb Castles",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Crystal_Castles/Walkthrough",
  "page_title": "Crystal Castles",
  "section_count": 4,
  "description": "Isometric Honeycomb Castles, Crystal Castles (More Atari 2600). Due to the games appearance right around the time when the home video game market was crashing, Crystal Castles did not see as wide a variety of home conversions as it might have, appearing primarily on Atari systems, but making its way to other popular home computers, courtesy of Atarisoft. Crystal Castlesis an arcade game released byAtariin1983.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Isometric Honeycomb Castles' from Crystal Castles (More Atari 2600). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Isometric Honeycomb Castles, Crystal Castles (More Atari 2600). Due to the games appearance right around the time when the home video game market was crashing, Crystal Castles did not see as wide a variety of home conversions as it might have, appearing primarily on Atari systems, but making its way to other popular home computers, courtesy of Atarisoft. Crystal Castlesis an arcade game released byAtariin1983. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "Crystal Castlesis an arcade game released byAtariin1983. It was released long after the stigma of appearing like aPac-Manclone had worn off. It began development as a much different game, a variant of theAsteroidstheme that would retain the 3D look that Crystal Castles ended up with. Much of the ideas for that game (intended to be called Toporoids) ended up in a different game,I, Robot, which was the first arcade game ever to contain filled 3D polygons. Crystal Castles became a more whimsical title, that also contained a number of arcade firsts, including a back-lit translucent track ball. Bentley Bear lives in a world of tree-dimensional perspective similar to that found inQ*BertorZaxxon, and he's the main character in what was one of Atari's most inventive games. Bentley's duty is to clear away all of the gems that cover the surface of each of the mazes, using elevators and ramps to cr",
  "brief": "Isometric Honeycomb Castles, Crystal Castles (More Atari 2600). Due to the games appearance right around the time when the home video game market was crashing, Crystal Castles did not see as wide a variety of home conversions as it might have, appearing primarily on Atari systems, but making its way to other popular home computers, courtesy of Atarisoft. Crystal Castlesis an arcade game released byAtariin1983.",
  "image_url": null,
  "image_kind": null,
  "image_urls": [],
  "image_kinds": []
 },
