 {
  "id": 122,
  "platform": "NES",
  "game": "Life Force",
  "target": "Organic Flesh Cavern",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Life_Force/Gameplay",
  "page_title": "Life Force",
  "section_count": 10,
  "description": "Organic Flesh Cavern, Life Force (NES). It began life as an arcade game where it was released in Japan under the nameSalamander(沙羅曼蛇,Salamander?). It was then re-adapted back to Japan under the same new title with a more organic theme. In Japan, theFamicomconversion of the game retained the original title ofSalamander, while outside of Japan, it was released asLife Force.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Organic Flesh Cavern' from Life Force (NES). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Organic Flesh Cavern, Life Force (NES). It began life as an arcade game where it was released in Japan under the nameSalamander(沙羅曼蛇,Salamander?). It was then re-adapted back to Japan under the same new title with a more organic theme. In Japan, theFamicomconversion of the game retained the original title ofSalamander, while outside of Japan, it was released asLife Force. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "Life Forceis the North American name of the game which is a spin-off of the originalGradiusgame. It began life as an arcade game where it was released in Japan under the nameSalamander(沙羅曼蛇,Salamander?). It was brought to the United States asLife Force. It was then re-adapted back to Japan under the same new title with a more organic theme. For more information about the arcade game and its various versions see theSalamanderguide. This game was converted for many popular systems, including theNES. In Japan, theFamicomconversion of the game retained the original title ofSalamander, while outside of Japan, it was released asLife Force. While this conversion retains most of the contents of the arcade version, some changes were made for this release. Like the arcade game, it contains two-player cooperative gameplay, both horizontally and vertically scrolling stages, and the ability to resume",
  "brief": "Organic Flesh Cavern, Life Force (NES). It began life as an arcade game where it was released in Japan under the nameSalamander(沙羅曼蛇,Salamander?). It was then re-adapted back to Japan under the same new title with a more organic theme. In Japan, theFamicomconversion of the game retained the original title ofSalamander, while outside of Japan, it was released asLife Force.",
  "image_url": null,
  "image_kind": null,
  "image_urls": [],
  "image_kinds": []
 },
 {
  "id": 123,
  "platform": "NES",
  "game": "Gradius II",
  "target": "Solar Prominence Corridor",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Gradius_II/Gameplay",
  "page_title": "Gradius II",
  "section_count": 9,
  "description": "Solar Prominence Corridor, Gradius II (NES). While the subtitle is present on many home conversions, it was specifically omitted for this one. It was developed and published byKonamiin Japan near the end of1988. Gradius II(グラディウスII,Gradius II?) is theFamicomconversion of the originalarcadeshooterknown asGradius II: Gofer no Yabou.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Solar Prominence Corridor' from Gradius II (NES). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Solar Prominence Corridor, Gradius II (NES). While the subtitle is present on many home conversions, it was specifically omitted for this one. It was developed and published byKonamiin Japan near the end of1988. Gradius II(グラディウスII,Gradius II?) is theFamicomconversion of the originalarcadeshooterknown asGradius II: Gofer no Yabou. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "Gradius II(グラディウスII,Gradius II?) is theFamicomconversion of the originalarcadeshooterknown asGradius II: Gofer no Yabou. While the subtitle is present on many home conversions, it was specifically omitted for this one. It was developed and published byKonamiin Japan near the end of1988. The conversion was developed in cooperation with the arcade development staff. Due to the limitations of the hardware, the Famicom conversion omits some stages from the arcade and rearranges others. Some of the background music differs from stage to stage as well. All that being said, the conversion is considered quite remarkable, and pushes the Famicom hardware's capabilities to the max. This conversion was made available on theWii Virtual Consolein Japan, alongside the more arcade faithful conversion for thePC Engine.",
  "brief": "Solar Prominence Corridor, Gradius II (NES). While the subtitle is present on many home conversions, it was specifically omitted for this one. It was developed and published byKonamiin Japan near the end of1988. Gradius II(グラディウスII,Gradius II?) is theFamicomconversion of the originalarcadeshooterknown asGradius II: Gofer no Yabou.",
