  "description": "Slum Turf & Mountain Temple, Double Dragon (NES). Home versions of the game were released for theNES,Sega Master System,Atari 2600,Atari 7800,Atari ST,Amiga,Commodore 64,Game Boy,Genesis/Mega DriveandAtari Lynx, among other platforms during the series's height of popularity. Another remake has been released for theiPodTouch/iPhone mobile devices, which features brand new gameplay, sprites and animations, and music. This is the first game in theDouble Dragonseries.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Slum Turf & Mountain Temple' from Double Dragon (NES). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Slum Turf & Mountain Temple, Double Dragon (NES). Home versions of the game were released for theNES,Sega Master System,Atari 2600,Atari 7800,Atari ST,Amiga,Commodore 64,Game Boy,Genesis/Mega DriveandAtari Lynx, among other platforms during the series's height of popularity. Another remake has been released for theiPodTouch/iPhone mobile devices, which features brand new gameplay, sprites and animations, and music. This is the first game in theDouble Dragonseries. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "This is the first game in theDouble Dragonseries. For other games in the series see theDouble Dragon category. Double Dragon(双截龍,Double Dragon?)is a1987beat 'em up developed byTechnos Japanand distributed in North America and Europe byTaito Corporation. The game is a spiritual and technological successor to Technos' earlier beat 'em up,Nekketsu Kōha Kunio-kun(released outside of Japan by Taito as Renegade), but introduced several additions such as two-player cooperative gameplay and the ability to arm oneself with an enemy's weapon after disarming them. Double Dragon is considered to be one of the first successful examples of the genre, resulting in the creation of two arcade sequels and several spinoffs, as well as inspiring other companies in creating their own beat 'em ups. The player takes control of martial artist Billy Lee, or his twin brother Jimmy, as they fight their way into th",
  "brief": "Slum Turf & Mountain Temple, Double Dragon (NES). Home versions of the game were released for theNES,Sega Master System,Atari 2600,Atari 7800,Atari ST,Amiga,Commodore 64,Game Boy,Genesis/Mega DriveandAtari Lynx, among other platforms during the series's height of popularity. Another remake has been released for theiPodTouch/iPhone mobile devices, which features brand new gameplay, sprites and animations, and music. This is the first game in theDouble Dragonseries.",
  "image_url": null,
  "image_kind": null,
