  "target": "High School & Shopping",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/River_City_Ransom",
  "page_title": "River City Ransom",
  "section_count": 1,
  "description": "High School & Shopping, River City Ransom (NES). River City Ransom(ダウンタウン熱血物語,Downtown Nekketsu Monogatari?, \"Downtown Hot-blooded Story\"), later released as Street Gangs in the PAL regions, is an open worldactionrole-playingbeat 'em upgame for theNES. Like its predecessors,River City Ransomunderwent great changes in its storyline and graphical presentation during its localization in order to make the game more palatable in the Western market.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'High School & Shopping' from River City Ransom (NES). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: High School & Shopping, River City Ransom (NES). River City Ransom(ダウンタウン熱血物語,Downtown Nekketsu Monogatari?, \"Downtown Hot-blooded Story\"), later released as Street Gangs in the PAL regions, is an open worldactionrole-playingbeat 'em upgame for theNES. Like its predecessors,River City Ransomunderwent great changes in its storyline and graphical presentation during its localization in order to make the game more palatable in the Western market. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "River City Ransom(ダウンタウン熱血物語,Downtown Nekketsu Monogatari?, \"Downtown Hot-blooded Story\"), later released as Street Gangs in the PAL regions, is an open worldactionrole-playingbeat 'em upgame for theNES. It was developed byTechnos Japanand originally released in Japan on April 25, 1989. It is the third game in Technos'Kunio-kunseries released for the console, preceded byRenegadeandSuper Dodge Ball. Like its predecessors,River City Ransomunderwent great changes in its storyline and graphical presentation during its localization in order to make the game more palatable in the Western market. It was one of the first console games published by North American subsidiary American Technos. Remakes of the game have been released for theSharp X68000,PC-Engine Super CD-ROM², andGame Boy Advance. The NES version was re-released for the NintendoWii Virtual Consolein 2007 as well as the NintendoWii U",
  "brief": "High School & Shopping, River City Ransom (NES). River City Ransom(ダウンタウン熱血物語,Downtown Nekketsu Monogatari?, \"Downtown Hot-blooded Story\"), later released as Street Gangs in the PAL regions, is an open worldactionrole-playingbeat 'em upgame for theNES. Like its predecessors,River City Ransomunderwent great changes in its storyline and graphical presentation during its localization in order to make the game more palatable in the Western market.",
