  "id": 172,
  "platform": "Sega Genesis & Master System",
  "game": "Sonic & Knuckles",
  "target": "Flying Battery Zone",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Sonic_%26_Knuckles/Walkthrough",
  "page_title": "Sonic & Knuckles",
  "section_count": 21,
  "description": "Flying Battery Zone, Sonic & Knuckles (Sega Genesis & Master System). The game features unique \"lock-on technology\" which enables another cartridge to be plugged in via the socket on top. Sonic & Knucklesis aplatformgame in theSonic the Hedgehogseries, developed bySonic Teamin collaboration with Sega Technical Institute, and published bySegafor theSega Genesisin1994. It is the direct sequel toSonic the Hedgehog 3, which was released earlier that year.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Flying Battery Zone' from Sonic & Knuckles (Sega Genesis & Master System). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Flying Battery Zone, Sonic & Knuckles (Sega Genesis & Master System). The game features unique \"lock-on technology\" which enables another cartridge to be plugged in via the socket on top. Sonic & Knucklesis aplatformgame in theSonic the Hedgehogseries, developed bySonic Teamin collaboration with Sega Technical Institute, and published bySegafor theSega Genesisin1994. It is the direct sequel toSonic the Hedgehog 3, which was released earlier that year. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "Sonic & Knucklesis aplatformgame in theSonic the Hedgehogseries, developed bySonic Teamin collaboration with Sega Technical Institute, and published bySegafor theSega Genesisin1994. It is the direct sequel toSonic the Hedgehog 3, which was released earlier that year. The game features unique \"lock-on technology\" which enables another cartridge to be plugged in via the socket on top. This allows for Knuckles to be used inSonic the Hedgehog 2and linksSonic the Hedgehog 3andSonic & Knucklestogether intoSonic the Hedgehog 3 & Knuckles. It was released onWindowsviaSteamasSonic 3 & Knuckles, though the title screen saysSonic 3 Sonic The Hedgehog & Knuckles. The game was included in theSonic's Ultimate Genesis Collectioncompilation in2009for the PS3 and Xbox 360.",
  "brief": "Flying Battery Zone, Sonic & Knuckles (Sega Genesis & Master System). The game features unique \"lock-on technology\" which enables another cartridge to be plugged in via the socket on top. Sonic & Knucklesis aplatformgame in theSonic the Hedgehogseries, developed bySonic Teamin collaboration with Sega Technical Institute, and published bySegafor theSega Genesisin1994. It is the direct sequel toSonic the Hedgehog 3, which was released earlier that year.",
