 {
  "id": 173,
  "platform": "Sega Genesis & Master System",
  "game": "Streets of Rage 3",
  "target": "Robotic Assembly Plant",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Streets_of_Rage_3/Walkthrough",
  "page_title": "Streets of Rage 3",
  "section_count": 1,
  "description": "Robotic Assembly Plant, Streets of Rage 3 (Sega Genesis & Master System). Using a larger 24-megabit (3 megabyte) cartridge, it features more moves and characters, a more complex plot, multiple endings, and longer rounds than the previous games. Streets of Rage 3(Bare Knuckle IIIin Japan), first released in1994for theSega Genesis, is the third and final game in theStreets of Rageseries ofbeat 'em ups. It was later released onGameTap, and on theWii Virtual Consoleon September 24,2007.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Robotic Assembly Plant' from Streets of Rage 3 (Sega Genesis & Master System). World brief: Robotic Assembly Plant, Streets of Rage 3 (Sega Genesis & Master System). Using a larger 24-megabit (3 megabyte) cartridge, it features more moves and characters, a more complex plot, multiple endings, and longer rounds than the previous games. Streets of Rage 3(Bare Knuckle IIIin Japan), first released in1994for theSega Genesis, is the third and final game in theStreets of Rageseries ofbeat 'em ups. It was later released onGameTap, and on theWii Virtual Consoleon September 24,2007. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "Streets of Rage 3(Bare Knuckle IIIin Japan), first released in1994for theSega Genesis, is the third and final game in theStreets of Rageseries ofbeat 'em ups. Using a larger 24-megabit (3 megabyte) cartridge, it features more moves and characters, a more complex plot, multiple endings, and longer rounds than the previous games. As well as being far more difficult than its predecessors, it has also been criticized for having an abrasive and noisy soundtrack, more experimental than the previous two which used more melodies and dance beats. It was later released onGameTap, and on theWii Virtual Consoleon September 24,2007. It is also included in the Japanese version ofSonic Gems Collection(it was excluded from other regions to get lower age ratings).",
  "brief": "Robotic Assembly Plant, Streets of Rage 3 (Sega Genesis & Master System). Using a larger 24-megabit (3 megabyte) cartridge, it features more moves and characters, a more complex plot, multiple endings, and longer rounds than the previous games. Streets of Rage 3(Bare Knuckle IIIin Japan), first released in1994for theSega Genesis, is the third and final game in theStreets of Rageseries ofbeat 'em ups. It was later released onGameTap, and on theWii Virtual Consoleon September 24,2007."
 },
