  "id": 179,
  "platform": "Sega Genesis & Master System",
  "game": "Earthworm Jim 2",
  "target": "Lorenzen's Soil Caverns",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Earthworm_Jim_2",
  "page_title": "Earthworm Jim 2",
  "section_count": 1,
  "description": "Lorenzen's Soil Caverns, Earthworm Jim 2 (Sega Genesis & Master System). Earthworm Jim 2is a run and gun platform video game starring an earthworm named Jim in a robotic suit who battles evil. It is a sequel to the originalEarthworm Jim, and the final game in the series developed by original creators Doug TenNapel, David Perry, and Shiny Entertainment. However, gameplay is much more diverse than in the first Earthworm Jim.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Lorenzen's Soil Caverns' from Earthworm Jim 2 (Sega Genesis & Master System). World brief: Lorenzen's Soil Caverns, Earthworm Jim 2 (Sega Genesis & Master System). Earthworm Jim 2is a run and gun platform video game starring an earthworm named Jim in a robotic suit who battles evil. It is a sequel to the originalEarthworm Jim, and the final game in the series developed by original creators Doug TenNapel, David Perry, and Shiny Entertainment. However, gameplay is much more diverse than in the first Earthworm Jim. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "Earthworm Jim 2is a run and gun platform video game starring an earthworm named Jim in a robotic suit who battles evil. It is a sequel to the originalEarthworm Jim, and the final game in the series developed by original creators Doug TenNapel, David Perry, and Shiny Entertainment. The purpose of the game is largely the same as it was in the original Earthworm Jim; traverse through the levels in order to save Princess What's Her Name, and defeat the game's numerous enemies, namely Psy-Crow. However, gameplay is much more diverse than in the first Earthworm Jim. While the majority of levels are still based on run and gun and platformer game elements, separate levels incorporate different gameplay elements as well.",
  "brief": "Lorenzen's Soil Caverns, Earthworm Jim 2 (Sega Genesis & Master System). Earthworm Jim 2is a run and gun platform video game starring an earthworm named Jim in a robotic suit who battles evil. It is a sequel to the originalEarthworm Jim, and the final game in the series developed by original creators Doug TenNapel, David Perry, and Shiny Entertainment. However, gameplay is much more diverse than in the first Earthworm Jim."
 },
