 {
  "id": 190,
  "platform": "Arcade",
  "game": "1942",
  "target": "Pacific Coral Atolls",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/1942/Walkthrough",
  "page_title": "1942",
  "section_count": 6,
  "description": "Pacific Coral Atolls, 1942 (Arcade). 1942 was picked up for distribution on several popular European home computers by Elite Systems, and was later relicensed for distribution by Encore. ASCII Corporation brought 1942 to home computers in Japan by porting the game to the MSX1 computer system, and later releasing a graphically updated version for the more capable MSX2 computer system. AmongCapcom's earliest games, 1942 was one of the most successful.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Pacific Coral Atolls' from 1942 (Arcade). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Pacific Coral Atolls, 1942 (Arcade). 1942 was picked up for distribution on several popular European home computers by Elite Systems, and was later relicensed for distribution by Encore. ASCII Corporation brought 1942 to home computers in Japan by porting the game to the MSX1 computer system, and later releasing a graphically updated version for the more capable MSX2 computer system. AmongCapcom's earliest games, 1942 was one of the most successful. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "1942is considered to be one of the defining games of the vertically scrolling shooter genre. AmongCapcom's earliest games, 1942 was one of the most successful. The subject of the game isn't hard to figure out. You play as an American pilot pitted against the entire Japanese Air Force during World War II in the titular year. Following the format established byXevious, enemies come out in periodic waves, taking shots at your plane before turning around and attempting to escape with their lives. Larger aircraft that require more shots to destroy appear less frequently and add to the challenge by blocking shots fired at enemies higher up the screen. Besides shooting, the player can also perform a 'loop-de-loop' to avoid enemy projectiles. 1942 incorporates a few power-ups that can help increase your plane's firepower, while also increasing your exposure. 1942 was picked up for distribution o",
  "brief": "Pacific Coral Atolls, 1942 (Arcade). 1942 was picked up for distribution on several popular European home computers by Elite Systems, and was later relicensed for distribution by Encore. ASCII Corporation brought 1942 to home computers in Japan by porting the game to the MSX1 computer system, and later releasing a graphically updated version for the more capable MSX2 computer system. AmongCapcom's earliest games, 1942 was one of the most successful.",
  "image_url": null,
  "image_kind": null,
  "image_urls": [],
  "image_kinds": []
 },
 {
  "id": 191,
  "platform": "Arcade",
  "game": "Time Pilot",
  "target": "1910 Airspace to 2001 Orbit",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Time_Pilot/Walkthrough",
  "page_title": "Time Pilot",
  "section_count": 7,
  "description": "1910 Airspace to 2001 Orbit, Time Pilot (Arcade). Coleco purchased the rights to publish the game for home consoles, while Konami proceeded to publish the game on the popularMSXcomputer system in Japan. This is the first game in theTime Pilotseries. For other games in the series see theTime Pilot category.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing '1910 Airspace to 2001 Orbit' from Time Pilot (Arcade). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: 1910 Airspace to 2001 Orbit, Time Pilot (Arcade). Coleco purchased the rights to publish the game for home consoles, while Konami proceeded to publish the game on the popularMSXcomputer system in Japan. This is the first game in theTime Pilotseries. For other games in the series see theTime Pilot category. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "This is the first game in theTime Pilotseries. For other games in the series see theTime Pilot category. Time Pilotis a1982arcade game byKonamiand distributed in the US byCenturi, designed by Yoshiki Okamoto. Yoshiki was told to design a driving game. When he learned of the game's concept, he balked at making it and started on Time Pilot. As development continued, Okamoto showed his boss design docs for the driving game, all the while working on Time Pilot. Although his boss told him to do the driving game instead, he tried to take the credit for Time Pilot. Okamoto decided not to disgrace his boss and let the matter drop. Time Pilot was successful due to its simplicity and non-stop intensity. Enemies came at you constantly, but your plane always seemed to be able wriggle out of tight spots. Coleco purchased the rights to publish the game for home consoles, while Konami proceeded to publ",
  "brief": "1910 Airspace to 2001 Orbit, Time Pilot (Arcade). Coleco purchased the rights to publish the game for home consoles, while Konami proceeded to publish the game on the popularMSXcomputer system in Japan. This is the first game in theTime Pilotseries. For other games in the series see theTime Pilot category.",
  "image_url": null,
  "image_kind": null,
  "image_urls": [],
  "image_kinds": []
 },
 {
  "id": 192,
  "platform": "Arcade",
  "game": "Galaga",
  "target": "Deep Space Swarm Horizon",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Galaga/Walkthrough",
  "page_title": "Galaga",
  "section_count": 10,
  "description": "Deep Space Swarm Horizon, Galaga (Arcade). However, despite its incredible popularity in the arcade, it saw comparatively few official home conversions in the United States. Galagais a spiritual successor toGalaxian. Several homebrew programmers have supplied alternate versions of this game stateside, while Japan saw an incredible number of conversions for popular computer models which were only available to in the \"Land of the Rising Sun\".",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Deep Space Swarm Horizon' from Galaga (Arcade). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Deep Space Swarm Horizon, Galaga (Arcade). However, despite its incredible popularity in the arcade, it saw comparatively few official home conversions in the United States. Galagais a spiritual successor toGalaxian. Several homebrew programmers have supplied alternate versions of this game stateside, while Japan saw an incredible number of conversions for popular computer models which were only available to in the \"Land of the Rising Sun\". Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "Galagais a spiritual successor toGalaxian. Developed and published byNamcoin Japan, and published byMidway Gamesin the US, Galaga seems to represent something of a \"sweet spot\" in game design, having performed better than either its predecessor or its successor,Gaplus(which was later renamed to \"Galaga 3\" when it was released in the United States to increase recognition and boost sales). However, despite its incredible popularity in the arcade, it saw comparatively few official home conversions in the United States. Several homebrew programmers have supplied alternate versions of this game stateside, while Japan saw an incredible number of conversions for popular computer models which were only available to in the \"Land of the Rising Sun\".",
  "brief": "Deep Space Swarm Horizon, Galaga (Arcade). However, despite its incredible popularity in the arcade, it saw comparatively few official home conversions in the United States. Galagais a spiritual successor toGalaxian. Several homebrew programmers have supplied alternate versions of this game stateside, while Japan saw an incredible number of conversions for popular computer models which were only available to in the \"Land of the Rising Sun\".",
