  "page_title": "Rampage",
  "section_count": 1,
  "description": "City High-Rise Block, Rampage (Arcade). They were ordinary humans (until they were mutated, by eating radioactive vitamins, taking a bath in a radioactive lake, and eating a 'scam' sausage respectively); their only goals now are to destroy every city they come across, and this game has 768 days of destruction (this game says \"no two are alike\", but the cycle repeats five times). This is the first game in theRampageseries.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'City High-Rise Block' from Rampage (Arcade). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: City High-Rise Block, Rampage (Arcade). They were ordinary humans (until they were mutated, by eating radioactive vitamins, taking a bath in a radioactive lake, and eating a 'scam' sausage respectively); their only goals now are to destroy every city they come across, and this game has 768 days of destruction (this game says \"no two are alike\", but the cycle repeats five times). This is the first game in theRampageseries. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "This is the first game in theRampageseries. For other games in the series see theRampage category. Rampageis an arcade game, that was released byBally Midwayin1986; it runs upon their MCR-3 hardware, but without those two General Instrument AY-3-8910s. The players must utilize an 8-way joystick to take control of one of three different monsters, with two buttons to make them punch and jump - George the giant gorilla, Lizzie the giant lizard, and Ralph the giant wolf. They were ordinary humans (until they were mutated, by eating radioactive vitamins, taking a bath in a radioactive lake, and eating a 'scam' sausage respectively); their only goals now are to destroy every city they come across, and this game has 768 days of destruction (this game says \"no two are alike\", but the cycle repeats five times). They must punch buildings and vehicles to destroy them as well as eat civilians that l",
  "brief": "City High-Rise Block, Rampage (Arcade). They were ordinary humans (until they were mutated, by eating radioactive vitamins, taking a bath in a radioactive lake, and eating a 'scam' sausage respectively); their only goals now are to destroy every city they come across, and this game has 768 days of destruction (this game says \"no two are alike\", but the cycle repeats five times). This is the first game in theRampageseries.",
