 {
  "id": 209,
  "platform": "Atari 2600 / 5200 / 7800",
  "game": "Ice Hockey",
  "target": "Symmetrical Indoor Ice Rink",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Ice_Hockey",
  "page_title": "Ice Hockey",
  "section_count": 1,
  "description": "Symmetrical Indoor Ice Rink, Ice Hockey (Atari 2600 / 5200 / 7800). Ice Hockeyis a game of two-on-twoice hockeydesigned byActivisionprogrammer Alan Miller, and published by Activision for theAtari 2600. One player on each team is the goalie, and the other plays offensive (although, the goalie is not confined to the goal). When the puck is in player control, it moves left and right along the blade of the hockey stick.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Symmetrical Indoor Ice Rink' from Ice Hockey (Atari 2600 / 5200 / 7800). The attached reference image is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Symmetrical Indoor Ice Rink, Ice Hockey (Atari 2600 / 5200 / 7800). Ice Hockeyis a game of two-on-twoice hockeydesigned byActivisionprogrammer Alan Miller, and published by Activision for theAtari 2600. One player on each team is the goalie, and the other plays offensive (although, the goalie is not confined to the goal). When the puck is in player control, it moves left and right along the blade of the hockey stick. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "Ice Hockeyis a game of two-on-twoice hockeydesigned byActivisionprogrammer Alan Miller, and published by Activision for theAtari 2600. One player on each team is the goalie, and the other plays offensive (although, the goalie is not confined to the goal). As in the real sport, the object of the game is to take control of the puck and shoot it into the opposing goal to score points. When the puck is in player control, it moves left and right along the blade of the hockey stick. The puck can be shot at any of 32 angles, depending on the position of the puck when it's shot. Human players take control of the skater in control of (or closest to) the puck. The puck can be stolen from its holder; shots can also be blocked by the blade of the hockey stick. In July 2010, Ice Hockey was made available onMicrosoft'sGame Roomservice for itsXbox 360console and for Games for Windows Live.",
  "brief": "Symmetrical Indoor Ice Rink, Ice Hockey (Atari 2600 / 5200 / 7800). Ice Hockeyis a game of two-on-twoice hockeydesigned byActivisionprogrammer Alan Miller, and published by Activision for theAtari 2600. One player on each team is the goalie, and the other plays offensive (although, the goalie is not confined to the goal). When the puck is in player control, it moves left and right along the blade of the hockey stick.",
  "image_url": null,
  "image_kind": null
 },
