 {
  "id": 221,
  "platform": "Atari 2600 / 5200 / 7800",
  "game": "Gorf",
  "target": "Astro Battles & Sub-Orbital Core",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Gorf/Walkthrough",
  "page_title": "Gorf",
  "section_count": 5,
  "description": "Astro Battles & Sub-Orbital Core, Gorf (Atari 2600 / 5200 / 7800). Namco subsequently forbid the Galaxian portion of the game to be included in any home conversion of the game, so most conversion contain only four stages. But there were still a few home conversions made, and they were quite popular. GORFis an arcade game released in1981byMidway Mfg..",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Astro Battles & Sub-Orbital Core' from Gorf (Atari 2600 / 5200 / 7800). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Astro Battles & Sub-Orbital Core, Gorf (Atari 2600 / 5200 / 7800). Namco subsequently forbid the Galaxian portion of the game to be included in any home conversion of the game, so most conversion contain only four stages. But there were still a few home conversions made, and they were quite popular. GORFis an arcade game released in1981byMidway Mfg.. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "GORFis an arcade game released in1981byMidway Mfg.. It was one of the first games in arcades to introduce multiple scenes in one game, beforeDonkey Kongbut afterPhoenix(1980). It is a multiple-mission fixed shooter with five distinct modes of play, essentially making it five games in one. It is also well-known for its use of synthesized speech, a new feature at the time. Midway still owned the rights to publishSpace InvadersandGalaxianin the United States and was looking for a way to make more money from those titles. Dave Nutting and Jay Fenton designed a game where the player could play through a series of space shooters instead of playing the same concept over and over again. In Gorf, which stands for \"Galactic Orbital Robot Force\", the player must take control of an attack ship that serves as the last line of defense between earth and the invading fleet. To accomplish the task of rid",
  "brief": "Astro Battles & Sub-Orbital Core, Gorf (Atari 2600 / 5200 / 7800). Namco subsequently forbid the Galaxian portion of the game to be included in any home conversion of the game, so most conversion contain only four stages. But there were still a few home conversions made, and they were quite popular. GORFis an arcade game released in1981byMidway Mfg..",
  "image_url": null,
  "image_kind": null,
  "image_urls": [],
  "image_kinds": []
 },
