  "target": "Open Kitchen Cafeteria Floor",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Food_Fight/Walkthrough",
  "page_title": "Food Fight",
  "section_count": 4,
  "description": "Open Kitchen Cafeteria Floor, Food Fight (Atari 2600 / 5200 / 7800). The XE version (which runs on all XL and XE home computers) is a bit poor as Charley runs far too quickly across the screen, but the 7800 version is hailed as a fabulous conversion, and among many 7800 owners' favorite games. Food Fightwas one of two games developed byGeneral Computer CorporationforAtarias the result of an out of court settlement between the two companies, the other beingQuantum.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Open Kitchen Cafeteria Floor' from Food Fight (Atari 2600 / 5200 / 7800). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Open Kitchen Cafeteria Floor, Food Fight (Atari 2600 / 5200 / 7800). The XE version (which runs on all XL and XE home computers) is a bit poor as Charley runs far too quickly across the screen, but the 7800 version is hailed as a fabulous conversion, and among many 7800 owners' favorite games. Food Fightwas one of two games developed byGeneral Computer CorporationforAtarias the result of an out of court settlement between the two companies, the other beingQuantum. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "Food Fightwas one of two games developed byGeneral Computer CorporationforAtarias the result of an out of court settlement between the two companies, the other beingQuantum. GCC started out by developing upgrade kits forMissile Commandwhich they sold to arcade owners without Atari's permission, so Atari sued. Food Fight was a \"cute\" game that pit a hungry young man named Charley Chuck against four hostile chefs. Charley's one and only goal, every stage, was to run from the right side of the screen over to the ice cream cone that was waiting for him, slowly melting, on the left side of the screen. Because the ice cream continued to melt, Charley only has 32 seconds to reach it before the ice cream is all gone. Between Charley and the cone are stockpiles of food and some angry chefs who are determined to prevent Charley from reaching the ice cream for some very unknown reasons. Charley wil",
  "brief": "Open Kitchen Cafeteria Floor, Food Fight (Atari 2600 / 5200 / 7800). The XE version (which runs on all XL and XE home computers) is a bit poor as Charley runs far too quickly across the screen, but the 7800 version is hailed as a fabulous conversion, and among many 7800 owners' favorite games. Food Fightwas one of two games developed byGeneral Computer CorporationforAtarias the result of an out of court settlement between the two companies, the other beingQuantum.",
  "image_url": null,
  "image_kind": null,
  "image_urls": [],
  "image_kinds": []
 },
