  "page_title": "The Battle of Olympus",
  "section_count": 2,
  "description": "Mount Olympus & Tartarus, The Battle of Olympus (NES). The Battle of Olympusis a side-scrolling action-adventure game for theNESdeveloped byInfinity. It was published in1988byImagineerin Japan for theFamicomand was titledOryunposu no Tatakai: Ai no Densetsu(オリュンポスの戦い 愛の伝説,The Olympus Fight: The Legend of Love?). The North American and European versions were released for the NES in1989and1991byBrøderbundand byNintendorespectively.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Mount Olympus & Tartarus' from The Battle of Olympus (NES). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Mount Olympus & Tartarus, The Battle of Olympus (NES). The Battle of Olympusis a side-scrolling action-adventure game for theNESdeveloped byInfinity. It was published in1988byImagineerin Japan for theFamicomand was titledOryunposu no Tatakai: Ai no Densetsu(オリュンポスの戦い 愛の伝説,The Olympus Fight: The Legend of Love?). The North American and European versions were released for the NES in1989and1991byBrøderbundand byNintendorespectively. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "The Battle of Olympusis a side-scrolling action-adventure game for theNESdeveloped byInfinity. It was published in1988byImagineerin Japan for theFamicomand was titledOryunposu no Tatakai: Ai no Densetsu(オリュンポスの戦い 愛の伝説,The Olympus Fight: The Legend of Love?). The North American and European versions were released for the NES in1989and1991byBrøderbundand byNintendorespectively. There's also a1993Game Boyport that was developed byRadical Entertainmentand published by Imagineer exclusively in Europe.",
  "brief": "Mount Olympus & Tartarus, The Battle of Olympus (NES). The Battle of Olympusis a side-scrolling action-adventure game for theNESdeveloped byInfinity. It was published in1988byImagineerin Japan for theFamicomand was titledOryunposu no Tatakai: Ai no Densetsu(オリュンポスの戦い 愛の伝説,The Olympus Fight: The Legend of Love?). The North American and European versions were released for the NES in1989and1991byBrøderbundand byNintendorespectively.",
