  "page_title": "1943: The Battle of Midway",
  "section_count": 5,
  "description": "Open Pacific Ocean Flotillas, 1943: The Battle of Midway (NES). The goal is to attack the Japanese air fleet that bombed the American aircraft carrier, pursue all Japanese air and sea forces, fly through the 16 stages of play, and make their way to the Japanese battleship Yamato and destroy her.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Open Pacific Ocean Flotillas' from 1943: The Battle of Midway (NES). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Open Pacific Ocean Flotillas, 1943: The Battle of Midway (NES). The goal is to attack the Japanese air fleet that bombed the American aircraft carrier, pursue all Japanese air and sea forces, fly through the 16 stages of play, and make their way to the Japanese battleship Yamato and destroy her. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "The game is set in the Pacific theater of World War II, off the coast of the Midway Atoll. The goal is to attack the Japanese air fleet that bombed the American aircraft carrier, pursue all Japanese air and sea forces, fly through the 16 stages of play, and make their way to the Japanese battleship Yamato and destroy her. 11 of these stages consist of an air-to-sea battle (with a huge battleship or an aircraft carrier as the stage boss), while 5 stages consist of an all-aerial battle against a squadron of Japanese bombers with a mother bomber at the end.",
  "brief": "Open Pacific Ocean Flotillas, 1943: The Battle of Midway (NES). The goal is to attack the Japanese air fleet that bombed the American aircraft carrier, pursue all Japanese air and sea forces, fly through the 16 stages of play, and make their way to the Japanese battleship Yamato and destroy her.",
