  "description": "Prehistoric Volcanic Skies, Dragon Spirit: The New Legend (NES). Dragon Spirit: The New Legend(ドラゴンスピリット 新たなる伝説,Dragon Spirit: The New Legend?)is a pseudo sequel to the arcade gameDragon Spirit, which was developed byNow Productionsfor theFamicom and NES. It was first published in Japan byNamcoin1989, and then a year later in North America byBandai. The New Legendplays identically to the originalDragon Spirit.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Prehistoric Volcanic Skies' from Dragon Spirit: The New Legend (NES). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Prehistoric Volcanic Skies, Dragon Spirit: The New Legend (NES). Dragon Spirit: The New Legend(ドラゴンスピリット 新たなる伝説,Dragon Spirit: The New Legend?)is a pseudo sequel to the arcade gameDragon Spirit, which was developed byNow Productionsfor theFamicom and NES. It was first published in Japan byNamcoin1989, and then a year later in North America byBandai. The New Legendplays identically to the originalDragon Spirit. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "Dragon Spirit: The New Legend(ドラゴンスピリット 新たなる伝説,Dragon Spirit: The New Legend?)is a pseudo sequel to the arcade gameDragon Spirit, which was developed byNow Productionsfor theFamicom and NES. It was first published in Japan byNamcoin1989, and then a year later in North America byBandai. Taking place several years after the events of the original, it adds many of the levels from the arcade version alongside new stages, enemies, boss fights and cinematic cutscenes, alongside a brand-new storyline. The New Legendplays identically to the originalDragon Spirit. The player controls a dragon as it travels across a vertical-scrolling screen, shooting down enemies in the air and on the ground. As was typical of shoot-em-ups of the era, the player can locate power-ups to make themselves more powerful. The story opens with a flashback or dream sequence where a man transforms into a dragon. If the pl",
  "brief": "Prehistoric Volcanic Skies, Dragon Spirit: The New Legend (NES). Dragon Spirit: The New Legend(ドラゴンスピリット 新たなる伝説,Dragon Spirit: The New Legend?)is a pseudo sequel to the arcade gameDragon Spirit, which was developed byNow Productionsfor theFamicom and NES. It was first published in Japan byNamcoin1989, and then a year later in North America byBandai. The New Legendplays identically to the originalDragon Spirit.",
  "image_url": "https://cdn.wikimg.net/en/strategywiki/images/0/09/Dragon_Spirit_NES_screen.png",
