  "target": "Kitchen Countertops & Pool Tables",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Micro_Machines",
  "page_title": "Micro Machines",
  "section_count": 1,
  "description": "Kitchen Countertops & Pool Tables, Micro Machines (NES). This is the first game in theMicro Machinesseries. For other games in the series see theMicro Machines category. Micro Machines, released in1991on theNESand in1993on other formats, was the first game in the series and laid the foundation of the gameplay: a top-downracinggame with miniature vehicles.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Kitchen Countertops & Pool Tables' from Micro Machines (NES). World brief: Kitchen Countertops & Pool Tables, Micro Machines (NES). This is the first game in theMicro Machinesseries. For other games in the series see theMicro Machines category. Micro Machines, released in1991on theNESand in1993on other formats, was the first game in the series and laid the foundation of the gameplay: a top-downracinggame with miniature vehicles. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "This is the first game in theMicro Machinesseries. For other games in the series see theMicro Machines category. Micro Machines, released in1991on theNESand in1993on other formats, was the first game in the series and laid the foundation of the gameplay: a top-downracinggame with miniature vehicles. The race tracks are unconventionally themed. For example, some races take place on a billiard table while others occur in a garden. The cartridge itself was gold (black in Europe) with a switch at the bottom in order to be compatible with the American and European hardware. It was also released as an add-on to the Aladdin Deck Enhancer created byCodemasters.",
  "brief": "Kitchen Countertops & Pool Tables, Micro Machines (NES). This is the first game in theMicro Machinesseries. For other games in the series see theMicro Machines category. Micro Machines, released in1991on theNESand in1993on other formats, was the first game in the series and laid the foundation of the gameplay: a top-downracinggame with miniature vehicles."
 },
