  "page_title": "Monster in My Pocket",
  "section_count": 2,
  "description": "Oversized Living Room & Kitchen, Monster in My Pocket (NES). Monster in My Pocketis a platform game released for theNESby Konami, and is based on the franchise developed by Morrison Entertainment Group. The franchise was initially collectable toys, before expanding to other media, including collectable cards, comic books, and the video game. These two characters must stop the actions of the Warlock, who releases his henchmen to defeat the two heroes.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Oversized Living Room & Kitchen' from Monster in My Pocket (NES). World brief: Oversized Living Room & Kitchen, Monster in My Pocket (NES). Monster in My Pocketis a platform game released for theNESby Konami, and is based on the franchise developed by Morrison Entertainment Group. The franchise was initially collectable toys, before expanding to other media, including collectable cards, comic books, and the video game. These two characters must stop the actions of the Warlock, who releases his henchmen to defeat the two heroes. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "Monster in My Pocketis a platform game released for theNESby Konami, and is based on the franchise developed by Morrison Entertainment Group. The franchise was initially collectable toys, before expanding to other media, including collectable cards, comic books, and the video game. The game is a platformer, where the players may choose either the Vampire or the Monster. These two characters must stop the actions of the Warlock, who releases his henchmen to defeat the two heroes.",
  "brief": "Oversized Living Room & Kitchen, Monster in My Pocket (NES). Monster in My Pocketis a platform game released for theNESby Konami, and is based on the franchise developed by Morrison Entertainment Group. The franchise was initially collectable toys, before expanding to other media, including collectable cards, comic books, and the video game. These two characters must stop the actions of the Warlock, who releases his henchmen to defeat the two heroes."
