 {
  "id": 275,
  "platform": "NES",
  "game": "Destiny of an Emperor",
  "target": "Ancient Chinese Steppes & Walled Cities",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Destiny_of_an_Emperor",
  "page_title": "Destiny of an Emperor",
  "section_count": 2,
  "description": "Ancient Chinese Steppes & Walled Cities, Destiny of an Emperor (NES). Destiny of an Emperor, known in Japan asTenchi wo Kurau(天地を喰らう,Tenchi wo Kurau?\"The Devouring of Heaven and Earth\"), is a strategyRPGbyCapcomfor theNES, originally released in Japan in1989, with an English language localization released for the North American market in1990. Additionally, most of these unique units can be recruited. Once recruited, the general will no longer be encountered in random battles.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Ancient Chinese Steppes & Walled Cities' from Destiny of an Emperor (NES). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Ancient Chinese Steppes & Walled Cities, Destiny of an Emperor (NES). Destiny of an Emperor, known in Japan asTenchi wo Kurau(天地を喰らう,Tenchi wo Kurau?\"The Devouring of Heaven and Earth\"), is a strategyRPGbyCapcomfor theNES, originally released in Japan in1989, with an English language localization released for the North American market in1990. Additionally, most of these unique units can be recruited. Once recruited, the general will no longer be encountered in random battles. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "Destiny of an Emperor, known in Japan asTenchi wo Kurau(天地を喰らう,Tenchi wo Kurau?\"The Devouring of Heaven and Earth\"), is a strategyRPGbyCapcomfor theNES, originally released in Japan in1989, with an English language localization released for the North American market in1990. The game is based on Hiroshi Motomiya's manga,Tenchi wo Kurau, which follows the story of Chinese historical figure Liu Bei and his sworn brothers, Zhang Fei and Guan Yu. This story is loosely based upon the events in the 14th-century historical novel Romance of the Three Kingdoms by Luo Guanzhong, which itself was based on historical events and battles which occurred before and during the Three Kingdoms period of ancient China. Unlike virtually every other RPG released at the time or since, the non-boss battles of Destiny of an Emperor do not consist solely of encounters with generic units. While generic enemy units ",
  "brief": "Ancient Chinese Steppes & Walled Cities, Destiny of an Emperor (NES). Destiny of an Emperor, known in Japan asTenchi wo Kurau(天地を喰らう,Tenchi wo Kurau?\"The Devouring of Heaven and Earth\"), is a strategyRPGbyCapcomfor theNES, originally released in Japan in1989, with an English language localization released for the North American market in1990. Additionally, most of these unique units can be recruited. Once recruited, the general will no longer be encountered in random battles.",
  "image_url": "https://cdn.wikimg.net/en/strategywiki/images/7/75/Destiny_of_an_Emperor_NES_overworld.png",
  "image_kind": "screenshot",
