 {
  "id": 302,
  "platform": "SNES",
  "game": "Brawl Brothers",
  "target": "Ruined City Sewers & Military Airbase",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Brawl_Brothers",
  "page_title": "Brawl Brothers",
  "section_count": 2,
  "description": "Ruined City Sewers & Military Airbase, Brawl Brothers (SNES). It is the only known SNES game that features the Japanese version on the same cartridge, accessible through the use of a cheat code. It is the second game in theRushing Beatseries, succeeding the first game in the series, known asRival Turf!outside of Japan. Versions of the game's box in certain European countries promote the game asRival Turf 2.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Ruined City Sewers & Military Airbase' from Brawl Brothers (SNES). The attached reference image is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Ruined City Sewers & Military Airbase, Brawl Brothers (SNES). It is the only known SNES game that features the Japanese version on the same cartridge, accessible through the use of a cheat code. It is the second game in theRushing Beatseries, succeeding the first game in the series, known asRival Turf!outside of Japan. Versions of the game's box in certain European countries promote the game asRival Turf 2. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "Brawl Brothers, known in Japan asRushing Beat Run(ラッシング・ビート乱 複製都市,Rasshingu Biito Ran: Fukusei Toshi?, Rushing Beat Chaos: The City of Clones), is a side-scrollingbeat 'em upmade byJalecoin1992for theSNES. It is the second game in theRushing Beatseries, succeeding the first game in the series, known asRival Turf!outside of Japan. Versions of the game's box in certain European countries promote the game asRival Turf 2. It is the only known SNES game that features the Japanese version on the same cartridge, accessible through the use of a cheat code. The Japanese version of the game features different character names, no maze-like stages, an expanded ending sequence and the addition of a groin kick move for playable character Douglas Bild. The game was followed by the release ofThe Peace Keepersin1993.",
  "brief": "Ruined City Sewers & Military Airbase, Brawl Brothers (SNES). It is the only known SNES game that features the Japanese version on the same cartridge, accessible through the use of a cheat code. It is the second game in theRushing Beatseries, succeeding the first game in the series, known asRival Turf!outside of Japan. Versions of the game's box in certain European countries promote the game asRival Turf 2.",
  "image_url": null,
  "image_kind": null
 },
