  "page_title": "SimAnt",
  "section_count": 4,
  "description": "Backyard Subterranean Ant Colony Galleries, SimAnt (SNES). The ant colony must battle against enemy red ants. The ultimate goal is to spread throughout the garden, into the house, and finally to drive out the antlions, spiders and human owners. In this respect, SimAnt differed from other Sim games that were open-ended and had no victory conditions.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Backyard Subterranean Ant Colony Galleries' from SimAnt (SNES). World brief: Backyard Subterranean Ant Colony Galleries, SimAnt (SNES). The ant colony must battle against enemy red ants. The ultimate goal is to spread throughout the garden, into the house, and finally to drive out the antlions, spiders and human owners. In this respect, SimAnt differed from other Sim games that were open-ended and had no victory conditions. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "In SimAnt, the player plays the role of an ant in a colony of black ants in the back yard of a suburban home. The ant colony must battle against enemy red ants. The ultimate goal is to spread throughout the garden, into the house, and finally to drive out the antlions, spiders and human owners. In this respect, SimAnt differed from other Sim games that were open-ended and had no victory conditions.",
