  "platform": "SNES",
  "game": "Blackthorne",
  "target": "Tuul Underground Slave Mines",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Blackthorne",
  "page_title": "Blackthorne",
  "section_count": 3,
  "description": "Tuul Underground Slave Mines, Blackthorne (SNES). Years before the game begins, Thoros, the latest ruler, finds it near impossible to choose between his two sons as the next ruler. Believing it will solve the dilemma, he leads them to the deserts and kills himself. He forms an army and leads them against Androth.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Tuul Underground Slave Mines' from Blackthorne (SNES). World brief: Tuul Underground Slave Mines, Blackthorne (SNES). Years before the game begins, Thoros, the latest ruler, finds it near impossible to choose between his two sons as the next ruler. Believing it will solve the dilemma, he leads them to the deserts and kills himself. He forms an army and leads them against Androth. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "Blackthorneis set on the planet Tuul, which has existed for hundreds of years without human knowledge. All of this time, Tuul's people have been ruled over by a single shaman who \"was blessed with all knowledge\". Years before the game begins, Thoros, the latest ruler, finds it near impossible to choose between his two sons as the next ruler. Believing it will solve the dilemma, he leads them to the deserts and kills himself. His body becomes two stones, light and dark, and he gives one to each boy to rule their own kingdoms respectively. The people of the lightstone form the kingdom of Androth, and the people of the Darkstone form Ka'dra'suul. But while Androth respects their stone, Ka'dra'suul reject theirs, and are eventually transformed into monsters by it. In this time, a ka'dra named Sarlac seizes power. He forms an army and leads them against Androth. Knowing of his people's doom, ",
  "brief": "Tuul Underground Slave Mines, Blackthorne (SNES). Years before the game begins, Thoros, the latest ruler, finds it near impossible to choose between his two sons as the next ruler. Believing it will solve the dilemma, he leads them to the deserts and kills himself. He forms an army and leads them against Androth."
 },
