  "description": "Steampunk Zeppelin Fleets & Steam Trains, Steel Empire (Sega Genesis / Master System / Game Gear). The levels also feature less powerful mini-bosses, which appear about halfway through a level. Steel Empire(Empire of Steelin Europe) is a side-scrollingshooter. Originally developed byHOT-Bunder the titleKoutetsu Teikoku(鋼鉄帝国,Koutetsu Teikoku?), it was brought to Europe and North America in1992byAcclaim's labelFlying Edge.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Steampunk Zeppelin Fleets & Steam Trains' from Steel Empire (Sega Genesis / Master System / Game Gear). The attached reference image is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Steampunk Zeppelin Fleets & Steam Trains, Steel Empire (Sega Genesis / Master System / Game Gear). The levels also feature less powerful mini-bosses, which appear about halfway through a level. Steel Empire(Empire of Steelin Europe) is a side-scrollingshooter. Originally developed byHOT-Bunder the titleKoutetsu Teikoku(鋼鉄帝国,Koutetsu Teikoku?), it was brought to Europe and North America in1992byAcclaim's labelFlying Edge. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "Steel Empire(Empire of Steelin Europe) is a side-scrollingshooter. Originally developed byHOT-Bunder the titleKoutetsu Teikoku(鋼鉄帝国,Koutetsu Teikoku?), it was brought to Europe and North America in1992byAcclaim's labelFlying Edge. A remake featuring technical upgrades saw the light in2004for theGame Boy Advancein Japan and Europe. The player can choose to fly the Striker Plane or the Z-01 Zeppelin to combat enemy fighters through seven progressively harder levels, each containing a boss character at the end, which must be defeated in order to advance to the next level. The levels also feature less powerful mini-bosses, which appear about halfway through a level. Steel Empire is notable amongst shooter games for its unique aesthetic designs. Mostly low-tech in nature, the game's environments are heavily stylized, with a steampunk theme to the technology. Steam power, propeller-based aircr",
  "brief": "Steampunk Zeppelin Fleets & Steam Trains, Steel Empire (Sega Genesis / Master System / Game Gear). The levels also feature less powerful mini-bosses, which appear about halfway through a level. Steel Empire(Empire of Steelin Europe) is a side-scrollingshooter. Originally developed byHOT-Bunder the titleKoutetsu Teikoku(鋼鉄帝国,Koutetsu Teikoku?), it was brought to Europe and North America in1992byAcclaim's labelFlying Edge.",
  "image_url": null,
