 {
  "id": 367,
  "platform": "Sega Genesis / Master System / Game Gear",
  "game": "Golden Axe II",
  "target": "Ancient Ruined Colosseums & Dragon Caves",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Golden_Axe_II/Gameplay",
  "page_title": "Golden Axe II",
  "section_count": 2,
  "description": "Ancient Ruined Colosseums & Dragon Caves, Golden Axe II (Sega Genesis / Master System / Game Gear). Unlike the original game, Golden Axe II has never been ported; although it did appear in the arcades on Sega's Mega-Tech and Mega Play hardware with some minor changes, theSega Genesis Collectionis its first appearance on another home system. The game builds upon the mechanics of the first game but features more responsive controls and different special moves.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Ancient Ruined Colosseums & Dragon Caves' from Golden Axe II (Sega Genesis / Master System / Game Gear). The attached reference image is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Ancient Ruined Colosseums & Dragon Caves, Golden Axe II (Sega Genesis / Master System / Game Gear). Unlike the original game, Golden Axe II has never been ported; although it did appear in the arcades on Sega's Mega-Tech and Mega Play hardware with some minor changes, theSega Genesis Collectionis its first appearance on another home system. The game builds upon the mechanics of the first game but features more responsive controls and different special moves. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "Golden Axe IIis a side-scrolling beat 'em up for theSega Genesis, and the Genesis sequel to the originalGolden Axe(the arcade sequelGolden Axe: The Revenge of Death Adderis unrelated). Unlike the original game, Golden Axe II has never been ported; although it did appear in the arcades on Sega's Mega-Tech and Mega Play hardware with some minor changes, theSega Genesis Collectionis its first appearance on another home system. Golden Axe II is a formulaic sequel: it sticks to the winning formula of the original game and does not deviate far from it. Unlike the first game a new villain, Dark Guld, has got hold of the titular Golden Axe and is wreaking havoc with it. The three characters from the original game (Gilius Thunderhead the dwarf, Ax Battler the barbarian, Tyris Flare the amazon) set out to stop him. The game builds upon the mechanics of the first game but features more responsive c",
  "brief": "Ancient Ruined Colosseums & Dragon Caves, Golden Axe II (Sega Genesis / Master System / Game Gear). Unlike the original game, Golden Axe II has never been ported; although it did appear in the arcades on Sega's Mega-Tech and Mega Play hardware with some minor changes, theSega Genesis Collectionis its first appearance on another home system. The game builds upon the mechanics of the first game but features more responsive controls and different special moves.",
  "image_url": null,
  "image_kind": null
 },
 {
  "id": 368,
  "platform": "Sega Genesis / Master System / Game Gear",
  "game": "Golden Axe III",
  "target": "Cursed Forest Glades & Whirlpool Falls",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Golden_Axe_III/Gameplay",
  "page_title": "Golden Axe III",
  "section_count": 6,
  "description": "Cursed Forest Glades & Whirlpool Falls, Golden Axe III (Sega Genesis / Master System / Game Gear). The storyline centers around a new villain known as Damud Hellbringer (or the Prince of Darkness) who has possessed the four heroes capable of saving Yuria. Golden Axe IIIis the last game in theGolden Axeseries before the radical changes ofGolden Axe: The Duel, and the speedy end of the series shortly after. The controls are more responsive than ever, and there are far more moves than in any previous game.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Cursed Forest Glades & Whirlpool Falls' from Golden Axe III (Sega Genesis / Master System / Game Gear). The attached reference image is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Cursed Forest Glades & Whirlpool Falls, Golden Axe III (Sega Genesis / Master System / Game Gear). The storyline centers around a new villain known as Damud Hellbringer (or the Prince of Darkness) who has possessed the four heroes capable of saving Yuria. Golden Axe IIIis the last game in theGolden Axeseries before the radical changes ofGolden Axe: The Duel, and the speedy end of the series shortly after. The controls are more responsive than ever, and there are far more moves than in any previous game. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "Golden Axe IIIis the last game in theGolden Axeseries before the radical changes ofGolden Axe: The Duel, and the speedy end of the series shortly after. It draws much of its inspiration fromGolden Axe: The Revenge of Death Adder, but has thrown out some ofGolden Axe II's improvements in the process. The controls are more responsive than ever, and there are far more moves than in any previous game. The storyline centers around a new villain known as Damud Hellbringer (or the Prince of Darkness) who has possessed the four heroes capable of saving Yuria. Gilius Thunderhead frees the players' heroes from this enslavement and sends them to take down Hellbringer. Just like The Revenge of Death Adder, Gilius is not playable in this game. The game never saw a U.S. release in cartridge form, and despite later being available to theSega Channel's limited subscriber base many players and at least o",
  "brief": "Cursed Forest Glades & Whirlpool Falls, Golden Axe III (Sega Genesis / Master System / Game Gear). The storyline centers around a new villain known as Damud Hellbringer (or the Prince of Darkness) who has possessed the four heroes capable of saving Yuria. Golden Axe IIIis the last game in theGolden Axeseries before the radical changes ofGolden Axe: The Duel, and the speedy end of the series shortly after. The controls are more responsive than ever, and there are far more moves than in any previous game.",
  "image_url": null,
  "image_kind": null
 },
