  "page_title": "Marvel Super Heroes",
  "section_count": 0,
  "description": "Thanos' Cosmic Shrine & Asteroids, Marvel Super Heroes (Arcade). It features many superheroes and supervillains from the Marvel Comics line, including Spider-Man, Doctor Doom, and the Hulk. Anita was only accessible this way in the Japan version of the arcade, but they are all accessible in the home conversions of the game that are also unlocked by secret codes, after the game has been beaten once or with points inMarvel vs.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Thanos' Cosmic Shrine & Asteroids' from Marvel Super Heroes (Arcade). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Thanos' Cosmic Shrine & Asteroids, Marvel Super Heroes (Arcade). It features many superheroes and supervillains from the Marvel Comics line, including Spider-Man, Doctor Doom, and the Hulk. Anita was only accessible this way in the Japan version of the arcade, but they are all accessible in the home conversions of the game that are also unlocked by secret codes, after the game has been beaten once or with points inMarvel vs. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "Marvel Super Heroesis a fighting game developed byCapcom. Originally released in the arcade in1995on the CPS-2 arcade system, it was later ported to theSega SaturnandPlayStation. It features many superheroes and supervillains from the Marvel Comics line, including Spider-Man, Doctor Doom, and the Hulk. In addition, Psylocke and Wolverine return fromX-Men: Children of the Atom, along with boss characters Juggernaut and Magneto. The game is loosely based on the Infinity Gauntlet storyline, with the heroes and villains battling each other for the Infinity Gems. The sub-boss is Doctor Doom followed by the Thanos as the final boss, who steals whatever Gems the player had collected (at that point, all but the sixth gem, Mind) and attaches them to the Infinity Gauntlet, which grants Thanos ultimate power over reality. The gameplay is similar to X-Men: Children of the Atom, but with a simplified",
  "brief": "Thanos' Cosmic Shrine & Asteroids, Marvel Super Heroes (Arcade). It features many superheroes and supervillains from the Marvel Comics line, including Spider-Man, Doctor Doom, and the Hulk. Anita was only accessible this way in the Japan version of the arcade, but they are all accessible in the home conversions of the game that are also unlocked by secret codes, after the game has been beaten once or with points inMarvel vs.",
