 {
  "id": 423,
  "platform": "More Arcade",
  "game": "Rolling Thunder",
  "target": "Subterranean Secret Agent Compounds",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Rolling_Thunder/Gameplay",
  "page_title": "Rolling Thunder",
  "section_count": 2,
  "description": "Subterranean Secret Agent Compounds, Rolling Thunder (More Arcade). Albatross's mission is to save a missing female agent named Leila Blitz from a secret society named Geldra located in New York City. Albatross must travel through two different segments or \"stories\", both comprised of five stages, for a total of ten game stages. On each stage, Albatross can enter doors, to hide and take cover from enemies, as well jump over to higher or lower floors with rails, including stairs.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Subterranean Secret Agent Compounds' from Rolling Thunder (More Arcade). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Subterranean Secret Agent Compounds, Rolling Thunder (More Arcade). Albatross's mission is to save a missing female agent named Leila Blitz from a secret society named Geldra located in New York City. Albatross must travel through two different segments or \"stories\", both comprised of five stages, for a total of ten game stages. On each stage, Albatross can enter doors, to hide and take cover from enemies, as well jump over to higher or lower floors with rails, including stairs. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "The player takes control of \"Albatross\", a member of the WCPO's (World Crime Police Organization) \"Rolling Thunder\" espionage unit. Albatross's mission is to save a missing female agent named Leila Blitz from a secret society named Geldra located in New York City. Albatross must travel through two different segments or \"stories\", both comprised of five stages, for a total of ten game stages. On each stage, Albatross can enter doors, to hide and take cover from enemies, as well jump over to higher or lower floors with rails, including stairs. Albatross begins this game armed with a standard-issue pistol, which can be substituted with a fully automatic assault rifle that allows for continuous firing by holding down the firing button. Albatross can gain ammunition for either weapon, by entering doors which are marked \"bullets\" or \"arms\". Despite the presence of a life meter, Albatross can o",
  "brief": "Subterranean Secret Agent Compounds, Rolling Thunder (More Arcade). Albatross's mission is to save a missing female agent named Leila Blitz from a secret society named Geldra located in New York City. Albatross must travel through two different segments or \"stories\", both comprised of five stages, for a total of ten game stages. On each stage, Albatross can enter doors, to hide and take cover from enemies, as well jump over to higher or lower floors with rails, including stairs.",
  "image_url": null,
  "image_kind": null,
  "image_urls": [],
  "image_kinds": []
 },
 {
  "id": 424,
  "platform": "More Arcade",
  "game": "Rolling Thunder 2",
  "target": "Neo Geldra Desert Mansions & Docks",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Rolling_Thunder_2/Gameplay",
  "page_title": "Rolling Thunder 2",
  "section_count": 9,
  "description": "Neo Geldra Desert Mansions & Docks, Rolling Thunder 2 (More Arcade). The Geldra organization, who are now known as Neo-Geldra and led by a new leader named Gimdo, and thought to have been destroyed at the end of the original Rolling Thunder, has returned, and are destroying several of the world's satellites in outer space.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Neo Geldra Desert Mansions & Docks' from Rolling Thunder 2 (More Arcade). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Neo Geldra Desert Mansions & Docks, Rolling Thunder 2 (More Arcade). The Geldra organization, who are now known as Neo-Geldra and led by a new leader named Gimdo, and thought to have been destroyed at the end of the original Rolling Thunder, has returned, and are destroying several of the world's satellites in outer space. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "The Geldra organization, who are now known as Neo-Geldra and led by a new leader named Gimdo, and thought to have been destroyed at the end of the original Rolling Thunder, has returned, and are destroying several of the world's satellites in outer space. As with the original game, the players must take control of a member of Interpol's fictitious \"Rolling Thunder\" task force; two players can now play this game simultaneously, while a single player now has a choice: between former damsel-in-distress Leila Blitz (1-UP) or the returning hero Albatross (2-UP). Apart from their different visual appearances (including different hand-guns), both the characters play exactly the same (much like Yūichirō Tomari and Sunday Chin, from Namco's ownOrdyne- which was released two years earlier, and also ran on Namco System 2 hardware). The graphics are noticeably improved from the original game (given ",
  "brief": "Neo Geldra Desert Mansions & Docks, Rolling Thunder 2 (More Arcade). The Geldra organization, who are now known as Neo-Geldra and led by a new leader named Gimdo, and thought to have been destroyed at the end of the original Rolling Thunder, has returned, and are destroying several of the world's satellites in outer space.",
