  "id": 425,
  "platform": "More Arcade",
  "game": "Shinobi (Arcade)",
  "target": "Terrorist Warehouses & Bamboo Compounds",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Shinobi/Walkthrough",
  "page_title": "Shinobi/Walkthrough",
  "section_count": 1,
  "description": "Terrorist Warehouses & Bamboo Compounds, Shinobi (Arcade) (More Arcade). There is a bonus stage between each mission. Shinobi is a linear game. Only the first mission has 3 stages, while the remaining missions have 4 (for a total of 19 stages).",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Terrorist Warehouses & Bamboo Compounds' from Shinobi (Arcade) (More Arcade). World brief: Terrorist Warehouses & Bamboo Compounds, Shinobi (Arcade) (More Arcade). There is a bonus stage between each mission. Shinobi is a linear game. Only the first mission has 3 stages, while the remaining missions have 4 (for a total of 19 stages). Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "Shinobi is a linear game. You must clear 5 missions, with each mission consisting of 3 or 4 stages. Only the first mission has 3 stages, while the remaining missions have 4 (for a total of 19 stages). In every stage except for the final stage of each mission, you must find a rescue all of the children being held hostage. You cannot proceed to the next stage until you rescue all of them. Among the children hostages, there is one who possesses a power-up function. Upon rescuing this child, your shuriken attacks will switch to a gun attack, and punch and kick attacks will switch to a ninja sword attack. In the final stage of each mission, a boss enemy will appear. You can only proceed to the next mission by defeating the boss character. There is a bonus stage between each mission. These bonus stages have a 3D perspective. You can earn bonus points by defeating all the enemy ninjas that are ",
  "brief": "Terrorist Warehouses & Bamboo Compounds, Shinobi (Arcade) (More Arcade). There is a bonus stage between each mission. Shinobi is a linear game. Only the first mission has 3 stages, while the remaining missions have 4 (for a total of 19 stages)."
 },
