 {
  "id": 443,
  "platform": "More Arcade",
  "game": "The King of Dragons (Arcade)",
  "target": "Hydra Swamps & Wyvern Peaks",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/The_King_of_Dragons",
  "page_title": "The King of Dragons",
  "section_count": 2,
  "description": "Hydra Swamps & Wyvern Peaks, The King of Dragons (Arcade) (More Arcade). The setting is very similar to that of Dungeons & Dragons and other medieval fantasy worlds, with familiar monsters such as Orcs, Gnolls, Harpies, Wyverns, Cyclopes, and Minotaurs. The game has 16 levels, though many are quite short. Much likeKnights of the Round, King of Dragons featuresRPG-like leveling.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Hydra Swamps & Wyvern Peaks' from The King of Dragons (Arcade) (More Arcade). World brief: Hydra Swamps & Wyvern Peaks, The King of Dragons (Arcade) (More Arcade). The setting is very similar to that of Dungeons & Dragons and other medieval fantasy worlds, with familiar monsters such as Orcs, Gnolls, Harpies, Wyverns, Cyclopes, and Minotaurs. The game has 16 levels, though many are quite short. Much likeKnights of the Round, King of Dragons featuresRPG-like leveling. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "The King of Dragonsis a1991side-scrollingbeat 'em upbyCapcomin which players travel through the kingdom of Malus to defeat the monsters that have taken over, as well as their leader, the red dragon Gildiss. The setting is very similar to that of Dungeons & Dragons and other medieval fantasy worlds, with familiar monsters such as Orcs, Gnolls, Harpies, Wyverns, Cyclopes, and Minotaurs. The game has 16 levels, though many are quite short. Much likeKnights of the Round, King of Dragons featuresRPG-like leveling. Characters' health bars, range and other attributes increase as they level up. Along the way, different weapon and armor upgrades can also be picked up. The game was ported to theSNESin1994and is also part ofCapcom Classics Collection Vol. 2, released for thePlayStation Portablein2006.",
  "brief": "Hydra Swamps & Wyvern Peaks, The King of Dragons (Arcade) (More Arcade). The setting is very similar to that of Dungeons & Dragons and other medieval fantasy worlds, with familiar monsters such as Orcs, Gnolls, Harpies, Wyverns, Cyclopes, and Minotaurs. The game has 16 levels, though many are quite short. Much likeKnights of the Round, King of Dragons featuresRPG-like leveling."
 },
