  "id": 465,
  "platform": "More Arcade",
  "game": "Ghosts 'n Goblins",
  "target": "Cursed Graveyards & Demon Castle Keep",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Ghosts_%27n_Goblins/Gameplay",
  "page_title": "Ghosts 'n Goblins",
  "section_count": 5,
  "description": "Cursed Graveyards & Demon Castle Keep, Ghosts 'n Goblins (More Arcade). \"Demon World Village\"), it is commonly regarded as one of the most difficult video games to complete that has ever been made. Those who are skillful enough to reach and defeat the final boss the first time through are not treated to the ending of the game. Instead, they are sent back to the beginning of the game where they must fight through every stage all over again at a higher level of difficulty.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Cursed Graveyards & Demon Castle Keep' from Ghosts 'n Goblins (More Arcade). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Cursed Graveyards & Demon Castle Keep, Ghosts 'n Goblins (More Arcade). \"Demon World Village\"), it is commonly regarded as one of the most difficult video games to complete that has ever been made. Those who are skillful enough to reach and defeat the final boss the first time through are not treated to the ending of the game. Instead, they are sent back to the beginning of the game where they must fight through every stage all over again at a higher level of difficulty. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "This is the first game in theGhosts 'n Goblinsseries. For other games in the series see theGhosts 'n Goblins category. Ghost 'n Goblinsis a platform arcade game byCapcomin1985. Known in Japan asMakai-Mura(lit. \"Demon World Village\"), it is commonly regarded as one of the most difficult video games to complete that has ever been made. Those who are skillful enough to reach and defeat the final boss the first time through are not treated to the ending of the game. Instead, they are sent back to the beginning of the game where they must fight through every stage all over again at a higher level of difficulty. Only upon beating the game for the second time does the player get to see a (short) happy ending. In the game, the player controls a knight named Arthur, who must defeat zombies, demons and other undead creatures in order to rescue a princess. Along the way the player can pick up new w",
  "brief": "Cursed Graveyards & Demon Castle Keep, Ghosts 'n Goblins (More Arcade). \"Demon World Village\"), it is commonly regarded as one of the most difficult video games to complete that has ever been made. Those who are skillful enough to reach and defeat the final boss the first time through are not treated to the ending of the game. Instead, they are sent back to the beginning of the game where they must fight through every stage all over again at a higher level of difficulty.",
  "image_url": null,
  "image_kind": null,
  "image_urls": [],
  "image_kinds": []
 },
 {
  "id": 466,
  "platform": "More Arcade",
  "game": "SonSon",
  "target": "Classical Chinese Mountain Trails & Cloudscapes",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/SonSon/Walkthrough",
  "page_title": "SonSon",
  "section_count": 20,
  "description": "Classical Chinese Mountain Trails & Cloudscapes, SonSon (More Arcade). In order to do that, SonSon (and if present, pig partner TonTon) must travel across 20 long and increasingly dangerous sections, fighting off animals, monsters, and other enemies. This is the first game in theSonSonseries. For other games in the series see theSonSon category.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Classical Chinese Mountain Trails & Cloudscapes' from SonSon (More Arcade). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Classical Chinese Mountain Trails & Cloudscapes, SonSon (More Arcade). In order to do that, SonSon (and if present, pig partner TonTon) must travel across 20 long and increasingly dangerous sections, fighting off animals, monsters, and other enemies. This is the first game in theSonSonseries. For other games in the series see theSonSon category. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "This is the first game in theSonSonseries. For other games in the series see theSonSon category. SonSonis an arcade game released byCapcomin1984. It is a blend of a side scrolling action game and a shooter game. It is Capcom's tribute to a Chinese legend called \"Xiyou Ji\" (\"Journey to the West\") considered to be one of the four classic pieces of Chinese literature. The main character in Xiyou Ji is Sun Wukong, or, when you pronounce the words as if they were Japanese kanji, Son Gokuu. That is the same story that inspired the design of the character Son Goku from theDragon BallandDragon Ball Zseries. It is possible to play the game co-operatively with partner who plays as the pig TonTon (Zhu Wuneng in the original story). In the game, you control the monkey named SonSon in an attempt to reach the statue of Buddha. In order to do that, SonSon (and if present, pig partner TonTon) must trave",
  "brief": "Classical Chinese Mountain Trails & Cloudscapes, SonSon (More Arcade). In order to do that, SonSon (and if present, pig partner TonTon) must travel across 20 long and increasingly dangerous sections, fighting off animals, monsters, and other enemies. This is the first game in theSonSonseries. For other games in the series see theSonSon category.",
  "image_url": null,
  "image_kind": null,
  "image_urls": [],
  "image_kinds": []
 },
 {
  "id": 467,
  "platform": "More Arcade",
  "game": "Exed Exes",
  "target": "Alien Hive Megastructure Plating",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Exed_Exes/Walkthrough",
  "page_title": "Exed Exes",
  "section_count": 6,
  "description": "Alien Hive Megastructure Plating, Exed Exes (More Arcade). It was licensed to Memetron and released outside of Japan in the arcades asSavage Bees. Exed Exesis an arcade vertical shooter developed byCapcom. It uses similar hardware to Capcom's1942, but it is more of a spiritual successor to Capcom's earlier shooterVulgus.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Alien Hive Megastructure Plating' from Exed Exes (More Arcade). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Alien Hive Megastructure Plating, Exed Exes (More Arcade). It was licensed to Memetron and released outside of Japan in the arcades asSavage Bees. Exed Exesis an arcade vertical shooter developed byCapcom. It uses similar hardware to Capcom's1942, but it is more of a spiritual successor to Capcom's earlier shooterVulgus. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "Exed Exesis an arcade vertical shooter developed byCapcom. It was licensed to Memetron and released outside of Japan in the arcades asSavage Bees. It uses similar hardware to Capcom's1942, but it is more of a spiritual successor to Capcom's earlier shooterVulgus. It takes place in a science fiction alien hive where you must pilot your ship through many stages protected by insects, some as large as your craft, and some even larger. What made Exed Exes stand apart from other shooters, besides the high resolution graphics for its time, and the detailed use of parallax scrolling to indicate depth, was the fact that it was one of the earliest vertical shooters to allow for two player simultaneous play. Rather than waiting for one player to take his turn, two players could enjoy the game at the same time, and even work cooperatively to get further along in the game. The only system that Exed E",
  "brief": "Alien Hive Megastructure Plating, Exed Exes (More Arcade). It was licensed to Memetron and released outside of Japan in the arcades asSavage Bees. Exed Exesis an arcade vertical shooter developed byCapcom. It uses similar hardware to Capcom's1942, but it is more of a spiritual successor to Capcom's earlier shooterVulgus.",
