 {
  "id": 489,
  "platform": "More Arcade",
  "game": "Fantasy Zone",
  "target": "Pastel Alien Planetary Landscapes & Bases",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Fantasy_Zone/Gameplay",
  "page_title": "Fantasy Zone",
  "section_count": 3,
  "description": "Pastel Alien Planetary Landscapes & Bases, Fantasy Zone (More Arcade). The final level consists of fighting again all previous bosses in succession and then facing the final one. When all the bases are gone, the stage boss appears, who must be defeated in order to move on to the next level.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Pastel Alien Planetary Landscapes & Bases' from Fantasy Zone (More Arcade). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Pastel Alien Planetary Landscapes & Bases, Fantasy Zone (More Arcade). The final level consists of fighting again all previous bosses in succession and then facing the final one. When all the bases are gone, the stage boss appears, who must be defeated in order to move on to the next level. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "The player controls a sentient spaceship named Opa-Opa who fights nonsensical invader enemies in the titular group of planets, full of settings atypical of the traditional scrolling shooter and pastel colors; for that reason, it is occasionally dubbed a \"cute 'em up\". In the game, the player's ship is placed in a level with a number of bases to destroy. When all the bases are gone, the stage boss appears, who must be defeated in order to move on to the next level. There are eight stages, and in all of them, except the final one, the scroll is not fixed; the player can move either left or right and the scroll follows him, though the stage loops. The final level consists of fighting again all previous bosses in succession and then facing the final one.",
  "brief": "Pastel Alien Planetary Landscapes & Bases, Fantasy Zone (More Arcade). The final level consists of fighting again all previous bosses in succession and then facing the final one. When all the bases are gone, the stage boss appears, who must be defeated in order to move on to the next level.",
  "image_url": null,
  "image_kind": null,
  "image_urls": [],
  "image_kinds": []
 },
 {
  "id": 490,
  "platform": "More Arcade",
  "game": "Wonder Boy in Monster Land",
  "target": "Pororo Islands, Deserts & Dragon Castle",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Wonder_Boy_in_Monster_Land/Gameplay",
  "page_title": "Wonder Boy in Monster Land",
  "section_count": 2,
  "description": "Pororo Islands, Deserts & Dragon Castle, Wonder Boy in Monster Land (More Arcade). After enjoying over a decade of peace on Wonder Land following the defeat of the evil King by Tom-Tom, later bestowed the title \"Wonder Boy\", a fire-breathing dragon called the MEKA dragon appeared; he and his minions conquered Wonder Land, turning it into \"Monster Land\". The people, helpless due to their lack of fighting skill, call for Wonder Boy, now a teenager, to destroy the monsters and defeat the MEKA dragon.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Pororo Islands, Deserts & Dragon Castle' from Wonder Boy in Monster Land (More Arcade). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Pororo Islands, Deserts & Dragon Castle, Wonder Boy in Monster Land (More Arcade). After enjoying over a decade of peace on Wonder Land following the defeat of the evil King by Tom-Tom, later bestowed the title \"Wonder Boy\", a fire-breathing dragon called the MEKA dragon appeared; he and his minions conquered Wonder Land, turning it into \"Monster Land\". The people, helpless due to their lack of fighting skill, call for Wonder Boy, now a teenager, to destroy the monsters and defeat the MEKA dragon. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "The game is the sequel to the 1986 gameWonder Boyand takes place eleven years after the events in the previous game. After enjoying over a decade of peace on Wonder Land following the defeat of the evil King by Tom-Tom, later bestowed the title \"Wonder Boy\", a fire-breathing dragon called the MEKA dragon appeared; he and his minions conquered Wonder Land, turning it into \"Monster Land\". The people, helpless due to their lack of fighting skill, call for Wonder Boy, now a teenager, to destroy the monsters and defeat the MEKA dragon. The plot of Wonder Boy in Monster Land follows the events in its predecessor, Wonder Boy. The game's main protagonist is a young boy named Bock Lee Temjin, although his friends call him \"Tom-Tom\". In Wonder Boy Tom-Tom's girlfriend Tanya was kidnapped by the \"evil King\" and was taken to his woodland kingdom; Tom-Tom set out to the kingdom, defeated the evil Kin",
  "brief": "Pororo Islands, Deserts & Dragon Castle, Wonder Boy in Monster Land (More Arcade). After enjoying over a decade of peace on Wonder Land following the defeat of the evil King by Tom-Tom, later bestowed the title \"Wonder Boy\", a fire-breathing dragon called the MEKA dragon appeared; he and his minions conquered Wonder Land, turning it into \"Monster Land\". The people, helpless due to their lack of fighting skill, call for Wonder Boy, now a teenager, to destroy the monsters and defeat the MEKA dragon.",
  "image_url": "https://cdn.wikimg.net/en/strategywiki/images/3/39/WBML_screen_pce.png",
  "image_kind": "screenshot",
  "image_urls": [
   "https://cdn.wikimg.net/en/strategywiki/images/3/39/WBML_screen_pce.png"
  ],
  "image_kinds": [
   "screenshot"
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": 491,
  "platform": "More Arcade",
  "game": "Wonder Boy III: Monster Lair",
