  "page_title": "Wonder Boy III: Monster Lair",
  "section_count": 1,
  "description": "Seaside Dunes & Volcanic Chasms, Wonder Boy III: Monster Lair (More Arcade). Health is gained through collection of fruit and projectile weapons. Wonder Boy III: Monster Lair(ワンダーボーイIII モンスターレア,Wonder Boy III: Monster Lair?)is a side-scrollingactiongame developed byWestoneBit Entertainment that was originally released for thearcadesbySegain1988. It is the third game in theWonder Boyseriesand the last one released for the arcade.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Seaside Dunes & Volcanic Chasms' from Wonder Boy III: Monster Lair (More Arcade). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Seaside Dunes & Volcanic Chasms, Wonder Boy III: Monster Lair (More Arcade). Health is gained through collection of fruit and projectile weapons. Wonder Boy III: Monster Lair(ワンダーボーイIII モンスターレア,Wonder Boy III: Monster Lair?)is a side-scrollingactiongame developed byWestoneBit Entertainment that was originally released for thearcadesbySegain1988. It is the third game in theWonder Boyseriesand the last one released for the arcade. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "Wonder Boy III: Monster Lair(ワンダーボーイIII モンスターレア,Wonder Boy III: Monster Lair?)is a side-scrollingactiongame developed byWestoneBit Entertainment that was originally released for thearcadesbySegain1988. It is the third game in theWonder Boyseriesand the last one released for the arcade. A console adaptation was made byHudson Soft, released in 1989 in Japan for thePC Engine CD-ROM² Systemand the subsequent North American release on theTurboGrafx-CDdropped the 'Wonder Boy III' title. It was also converted and released by Sega for theMega Drivein Japan in 1990 and Europe in 1991. Both, the TurboGrafx-CD and Mega Drive versions have been re-released for theWiiVirtual Console. The game balances basic concepts found in both platformers and shooters. The player is able to jump and shoot projectiles from a sword. He must ride a flying dragon and confront a large boss throughout the second half of",
  "brief": "Seaside Dunes & Volcanic Chasms, Wonder Boy III: Monster Lair (More Arcade). Health is gained through collection of fruit and projectile weapons. Wonder Boy III: Monster Lair(ワンダーボーイIII モンスターレア,Wonder Boy III: Monster Lair?)is a side-scrollingactiongame developed byWestoneBit Entertainment that was originally released for thearcadesbySegain1988. It is the third game in theWonder Boyseriesand the last one released for the arcade.",
  "image_url": "https://cdn.wikimg.net/en/strategywiki/images/3/30/Wonder_Boy_III_Monster_Lair_ARC_screen.png",
