 {
  "id": 509,
  "platform": "NES / Famicom",
  "game": "Mega Man 4",
  "target": "Pharaoh Man Quicksand & Skull Man Wastes",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Mega_Man_4",
  "page_title": "Mega Man 4/Pharaoh Man",
  "section_count": 1,
  "description": "Pharaoh Man Quicksand & Skull Man Wastes, Mega Man 4 (NES / Famicom). It's off to the desert to fight the next one of Dr. The first section features sinking quicksand and assorted foes. Cossack's creations.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Pharaoh Man Quicksand & Skull Man Wastes' from Mega Man 4 (NES / Famicom). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Pharaoh Man Quicksand & Skull Man Wastes, Mega Man 4 (NES / Famicom). It's off to the desert to fight the next one of Dr. The first section features sinking quicksand and assorted foes. Cossack's creations. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "It's off to the desert to fight the next one of Dr. Cossack's creations. The first section features sinking quicksand and assorted foes. Fight your way through, and don't let the sand eat you alive. When you reach the pit, DO NOT fall in. Use the Rush Coil to jump over it, and go one screen further to the right. You'll find the Balloon item here, and skip a pretty good-sized chunk of the stage! The rest of the stage is pretty standard run-and-fire stuff. Just keep bringing the pain and you'll eventually reach the boss lair. Pharaoh Man is one tough guy. Seems like most robot masters have speed but lack power, or vice versa. This guy has the best of both worlds, which guarantees he will not be an easy boss. But if you've got his weakness, the Flash Stopper, he can be turned into a sitting duck. Activate it as soon as you enter his lair, stand before him, and rapid fire. Just keep rapid fi",
  "brief": "Pharaoh Man Quicksand & Skull Man Wastes, Mega Man 4 (NES / Famicom). It's off to the desert to fight the next one of Dr. The first section features sinking quicksand and assorted foes. Cossack's creations.",
  "image_url": null,
  "image_kind": null,
  "image_urls": [],
  "image_kinds": []
 },
 {
  "id": 510,
  "platform": "NES / Famicom",
  "game": "Mega Man 5",
  "target": "Gravity Man Shifts & Wave Man Canals",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Mega_Man_5",
  "page_title": "Mega Man 5/Gravity Man",
  "section_count": 1,
  "description": "Gravity Man Shifts & Wave Man Canals, Mega Man 5 (NES / Famicom). Another weird gravity stage. The gravity isn't low like it was in Star Man's level, but it's REVERSED at portions of the stage! This makes for some very interesting gameplay.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Gravity Man Shifts & Wave Man Canals' from Mega Man 5 (NES / Famicom). The attached reference imagery is the primary guide: match its layout, landmarks, colors and mood. World brief: Gravity Man Shifts & Wave Man Canals, Mega Man 5 (NES / Famicom). Another weird gravity stage. The gravity isn't low like it was in Star Man's level, but it's REVERSED at portions of the stage! This makes for some very interesting gameplay. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "Another weird gravity stage. The gravity isn't low like it was in Star Man's level, but it's REVERSED at portions of the stage! This makes for some very interesting gameplay. It's a rather typical stage apart from the obvious gravity gimmick, with spikes being the biggest threat. Be careful not to land on them! You'll find the Beat Letter near one of the \"gravity change\" bars, and you have to time a jump just right to reach it, without falling to your death. Don't despair, it's really not that hard to get to. Gravity Man himself is as strange as the stage he hides out in. He constantly changes the gravity in the room, firing at you and jumping around as he does so. You'll always be on the opposite surface as him, so you have to fire at him as the two of you cross each other en route to the other floor when he changes the gravity. He's weak to the Star Crash, but this is the hardest weapo",
  "brief": "Gravity Man Shifts & Wave Man Canals, Mega Man 5 (NES / Famicom). Another weird gravity stage. The gravity isn't low like it was in Star Man's level, but it's REVERSED at portions of the stage! This makes for some very interesting gameplay.",
  "image_url": "https://cdn.wikimg.net/en/strategywiki/images/thumb/5/58/Megaman5box_Japan.jpg/800px-Megaman5box_Japan.jpg",
  "image_kind": "screenshot",
