 {
  "id": 516,
  "platform": "NES / Famicom",
  "game": "Metal Gear",
  "target": "Building 1 Warehouses & Outer Heaven Silos",
  "url": "https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Metal_Gear",
  "page_title": "Metal Gear",
  "section_count": 2,
  "description": "Building 1 Warehouses & Outer Heaven Silos, Metal Gear (NES / Famicom). The game revolves around a special forces operative codenamed Solid Snake who goes into a solo infiltration mission into the fortified state of Outer Heaven to destroy Metal Gear, a bipedal walking tank capable of launching nuclear missiles from anywhere in the world. The official translation contains many examples of \"Engrish\", such as consistently misspelling \"destroy\" as \"destoroy\". under Konami's supervision.",
  "qwen_prompt": "Generate a fully interactive 3D WebGL Three.js world representing 'Building 1 Warehouses & Outer Heaven Silos' from Metal Gear (NES / Famicom). World brief: Building 1 Warehouses & Outer Heaven Silos, Metal Gear (NES / Famicom). The game revolves around a special forces operative codenamed Solid Snake who goes into a solo infiltration mission into the fortified state of Outer Heaven to destroy Metal Gear, a bipedal walking tank capable of launching nuclear missiles from anywhere in the world. The official translation contains many examples of \"Engrish\", such as consistently misspelling \"destroy\" as \"destoroy\". under Konami's supervision. Include lighting, fog, textures/materials, animated environmental elements, and mouse/touch orbit camera controls.",
  "description_raw": "This is the first game in theMetal Gearseries. For other games in the series see theMetal Gear category. Metal Gear(メタルギア,Metaru Gia?)is an overhead military action-adventure game originally released in1987byKonamifor theMSX2computer standard in Japan and parts of Europe. Considered to be the progenitor of the stealth game genre, it was also the first video game designed by Hideo Kojima, who also directed many of the laterMetal Gearsequels. The game revolves around a special forces operative codenamed Solid Snake who goes into a solo infiltration mission into the fortified state of Outer Heaven to destroy Metal Gear, a bipedal walking tank capable of launching nuclear missiles from anywhere in the world. Most of the radio messages were edited or removed in the English version, including Big Boss' comments on every item and weapon found by the player. According to a fan-translation projec",
  "brief": "Building 1 Warehouses & Outer Heaven Silos, Metal Gear (NES / Famicom). The game revolves around a special forces operative codenamed Solid Snake who goes into a solo infiltration mission into the fortified state of Outer Heaven to destroy Metal Gear, a bipedal walking tank capable of launching nuclear missiles from anywhere in the world. The official translation contains many examples of \"Engrish\", such as consistently misspelling \"destroy\" as \"destoroy\". under Konami's supervision."
 },
